/	LAST EDIT: 18-MAY-2014 CJL.

/	TAKEN FROM A 1978 P?S/8 SYSTEM TAPE IMAGE [KNOWN TO NOT BE A FINAL RELEASE].

/	THIS IS THE P?S/8 SYSTEM PROGRAM KNOWN AS "BIN" PROVIDED AS A CORE-IMAGE PROGRAM
/	ON ANY COMPLETE P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE.  PORTIONS OF "BIN" ARE DEVICE-DEPENDENT AND
/	MUST BE CONFIGURED FOR THE SAME HARDWARE AS THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER. [NOTE:
/	VARIOUS SYSTEM GENERATION METHODS HAVE ATTEMPTED TO DEFINE THE RELATIONSHIP
/	BETWEEN THE PORTIONS OF BIN THAT ARE DEPENDENT ON THE SAME HARDWARE AS THE
/	SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.  AN EXTENDED HANDLER DEFINITION WILL LIKELY BE
/	IMPLEMENTED TO ENCOMPASS ALL DEVICE DEPENDENCIES INCLUDING THE KEYBOARD MONITOR
/	REWIND [^R] AND UNLOAD [^T] COMMANDS.

/	IMBEDDED UTILITIES.

/	THE CORE-IMAGE PROGRAM "BIN" HAS ALTERNATE ENTRY POINTS FOR "GET" AND "START".
/	WHILE THE START FUNCTION HAS LITTLE IN COMMON WITH THE PRIMARY FUNCTION OF THE
/	"BIN" UTILITY, "GET" IS MERELY "BIN" WITH CERTAIN OPTIONS FORCED.  PROPER USAGE
/	DEPENDS ON ALLOWING THE OPTIONS TO DETERMINE THE DESIRED FUNCTIONALITY; THERE IS
/	NO OTHER IMPLICATION.  VARIOUS USEFUL [AND OTHERWISE] OPTIONAL PARAMETERS ARE
/	ALLOWED; THE USER IS ADVISED TO AVOID UNINTENDED INTERACTION OF OVERALL PASSED
/	PARAMETERS.

/	GROUPED DEFINITIONS.

/	DUE TO THE CONFUSING ARRAY OF USAGES OF THE "BIN" UTILITY, DEFINITIONS OF
/	CERTAIN OPTION GROUPINGS WILL BE PROVIDED FOR CLARITY.

/	1) STARTUP INFORMATION: THE STARTING ADDRESS IS SPECIFIED BY =XXXX ON THE
/	   COMMAND LINE INVOKING THE PROGRAM AS A 4-DIGIT ADDRESS IN THE RANGE OF
/	   0000-7776.  THE STARTING FIELD IS SPECIFIED AS A UNIQUE OPTION SWITCH IN THE
/	   RANGE OF /0 THROUGH /7; IF ALL 8 OPTION SWITCHES ARE NOT PASSED, FIELD 0 WILL
/	   BE USED BY DEFAULT.  THE PROGRAM WILL ISSUE A FATAL ERROR MESSAGE IF MORE
/	   THAN ONE STARTUP FIELD IS SPECIFIED.  THE PROGRAM WILL NOT BE LOADED AND THE
/	   PROGRAM WILL EXIT TO P?S/8.

/	   IT IS NOT POSSIBLE TO START ANY PROGRAM AT 7777 BY DESIGN.  P?S/8 COMMAND
/	   PROCESSORS WILL PASS THIS VALUE TO INDICATE THE PROGRAM LACKS A STATED
/	   STARTING ADDRESS.  A DEVICE-DEPENDENT LOCATION OF A SAFE HALT OPERATION WILL
/	   BE USED INTERNALLY; ONCE PROGRAMS ARE LOADED, THE USER MUST MANUALLY OPERATE
/	   THE COMPUTER.  [NOTE: DEBUGGING IS AVAILABLE BY USING THE "GET" COMMAND IN
/	   CONJUCTION WITH P?S/8 ODT.]

/	2) LOADING OPTIONS: THE REST OF THE OPTIONAL COMMAND SWITCHES ARE AVAILABLE FOR
/	   VARIOUS ADDITIONAL LOADING OPTIONS.  ANY AND ALL IMPLEMENTED OPTION SWITCHES
/	   ARE COMPLETELY CONTEXT-DEPENDENT, OFTEN CONSISTENTLY SUPPLYING ANALOGOUS
/	   FUNCTIONALITY AMONG SEVERAL DIFFERENT MODES OF OPERATION WHERE APPLICABLE.
/	   [NOTE: THE "BIN" UTILITY IS SUBJECT TO CHAINED PROGRAM OPERATION FROM THE
/	   P?S/8 PAL ASSEMBLER ["PAL"] AND THE P?S/8 BITMAP UTILITY ["MAP"].  THIS IS
/	   USED TO PROVIDE ASSEMBLE, MAP, LOAD AND GO OPERATION IN ANY COMBINATION.]  AS
/	   SUCH, CERTAIN COMMAND OPTION SWITCHES MAY BE PRESENT INVOKED BY AN EARLIER
/	   COMMAND INCLUDING CHAINING OPTIONS; BIN IS ALWAYS THE FINAL OPTION STAGE OF
/	   THE CHAINING OPERATIONS WHERE APPLICABLE.  [NOTE: CHAINING TO BIN IS NOT
/	   ALLOWED IF ASSEMBLY ERRORS WERE DETECTED.] [NOTE: IT IS POSSIBLE FOR "BIN" TO
/	   CHAIN TO ITSELF UNDER SPECIFIC CIRCUMSTANCES; THIS MAY BE RELEASE-DEPENDENT.]

/	3) BINARY PAPER TAPE DEFINITIONS: THE "BIN" UTILITY CAN INTERACT WITH BINARY
/	   PAPER TAPES DESIGNED FOR USE WITH STAND-ALONE LOADING PROGRAMS ON SYSTEMS
/	   MORE PRIMITIVE THAN THE MINIMUM REQUIREMENT FOR P?S/8 [WHICH INCLUDES AN
/	   APPROPRIATE STORAGE DEVICE].  PAPER TAPE CONFIGURATIONS WERE CREATED FOR
/	   COMPUTERS HAVING A CONSOLE TELETYPE WITH AN ASR OPTION [AUTOMATIC
/	   SEND-RECEIVER PAPER TAPE OPTIONS SUCH AS THE ASR-33 AND ASR-35 TELETYPES] OR
/	   SIMILAR MACHINES WITH A HIGH-SPEED PAPER TAPE READER/PUNCH UNIT.

/	   BINARY PAPER TAPE CONVENTIONS ARE IN THEORY IDENTICAL TO P?S/8 MEMORY
/	   RESTRICTIONS IN THAT ONLY 07600-07777 ARE RESERVED BY P?S/8 IN FIELD 0.
/	   [NOTE: THERE ARE KNOWN "ROGUE" PROGRAMS THAT VIOLATE THE BINARY PAPER TAPE
/	   CONVENTIONS DESPITE THESE WELL-KNOWN MEMORY BOUNDARIES.  REGRETTABLY, SOME OF
/	   THESE PROGRAMS ARE OFFICIAL DEC DIAGNOSTIC PROGRAMS WHICH CAN ONLY BE LOADED
/	   BY CERTAIN SUBSETS OF THE BINARY PAPER TAPE ENVIRONMENT; THESE DEFECTIVE
/	   PROGRAMS EXPECT TO LOAD INTO CERTAIN LOCATIONS WITHIN 07600-07777 ON THE
/	   DEFECTIVE NOTION THAT THESE LOCATIONS ARE SOMEHOW AVAILABLE; INEVITABLY THIS
/	   DYSFUNCTIONALITY CAN BE TRACED TO IGNORANCE REGARDING THE FULL SET OF RULES
/	   OF BINARY PAPER TAPE LOADING CONVENTIONS; CERTAIN BINARY PAPER TAPE LOADERS
/	   CANNOT LOAD THESE PROGRAMS DUE TO THE ATTEMPT TO USE A VERY SMALL AREA OF
/	   MEMORY THAT IS OFF LIMITS BY DEFINITION.  P?S/8 "BIN" HAS A PROVISIONAL
/	   METHOD TO ATTEMPT TO OVERCOME THESE PROBLEMS WITH VARIOUS TRADEOFFS [AND
/	   KLUDGES THAT ARE RELEASE-DEPENDENT].




/	   [NOTE: P?S/8 EXTENDED MEMORY RESTRICTIONS ARE CONFIGURATION-DEPENDENT AND CAN
/	   BE TOTALLY UNLIMITED UNLIKE OTHER OPERATING SYSTEMS SUCH AS OS/8 WHICH ALWAYS
/	   RESERVES X7600-X7777 FOR ANY EXTENDED MEMORY FIELD X.  FOR CERTAIN DEVICE
/	   CONFIGURATIONS, P?S/8 MAY RESERVE VARIOUS PORTIONS OF THE HIGHEST EXTENDED
/	   MEMORY FIELD.  THE DESIGN PHILOSOPHY IS TO PROVIDE THE LARGEST POSSIBLE
/	   CONTIGUOUS MEMORY WITHOUT KLUDGES WHEN ADDRESSED IN EITHER 12-BIT MODE OR
/	   15-BIT MODE SUCH AS USED BY VARIOUS FPP PROGRAMS, ETC.]





/ AS WELL AS MAP, LOAD AND GO
/	   OPERATION [AND ASSEMBLE, MAP 









/	DUE TO THE CONFUSING ARRAY OF OPTIONS AND EXTERNAL NAMES FOR CONCEPTS ASSOCIATED
/	WITH PDP-8 BINARY LOADING IN GENERAL, A SPECIAL GLOSSARY OF TERMS IS NEEDED:

/	P?S/8 "BIN" - THE NAME OF THIS P?S/8 CORE-IMAGE UTILITY PROGRAM.

/	BIN - THE NAME OF PAPER-TAPE FORMAT FOR LOADING PDP-8 BINARY FILES FROM PAPER
/	TAPES THAT USES CHECKSUMS AND AN AUTO-INCREMENTING LOADING POINTER.  THE
/	STAND-ALONE VERSION OF A LOADER FOR THIS FORMAT USES EITHER THE CONSOLE TELETYPE
/	READER IF THE CONSOLE IS AN ASR-33 OR ASR-35 OR EQUIVALENT, OR THE HIGH-SPEED
/	READER AS USUALLY IMPLEMENTED ALONG WITH A HIGH-SPEED PUNCH FOR THE SAME OVERALL
/	PAPER TAPE FORMAT.  THE OVERALL SET OF BIN UTILITIES IS MORE RELIABLE THAN
/	SHORTER EQUIVALENT METHODS, BUT TRADES OFF LONGER PROGRAMS FOR RELIABILITY.  FOR
/	CLARITY, BIN PAPER TAPE WILL ALWAYS BE USED WHEN REFERENCING ANY ASPECT OF THIS
/	FORMAT MEDIA.

/	RIM [READ-IN MODE] - THE NAME OF AN ALTERNATE PAPER-TAPE FORMAT FOR LOADING
/	PDP-8 BINARY FILES. SINCE THE FORMAT IS BASICALLY A SUBSET OF BIN PAPER TAPE
/	FORMAT, EVERY WORD LOADED INTO MEMORY REQUIRES AN ADDRESS BEFORE THE DATA.  AS
/	SUCH, THERE IS NO ADVANTAGE TAKEN OF SEQUENTIAL LOADING; THE PAPER TAPES WILL BE
/	SUBSTANTIALLY LONGER FOR EQUIVALENT FUNCTIONALITY.  THERE ARE ADDITIONAL
/	RESTRICTIONS WHEN USING RIM PAPER TAPE FORMAT: 1) NO CHECKSUMS ARE CALCULATED
/	THUS LOWERING OVERALL LOADING RELIABILITY, 2) BIN PAPER TAPE FORMAT SUPPORTS
/	LOADING FIELDS WITHIN THE DATA; INITIAL LOADING CAN BE OVERRIDEN ON THE CPU
/	FRONT PANEL, BUT IMBEDDED FIELD SETTINGS WILL OVERRIDE ANY FORM OF DEFAULT
/	SETTING.  RIM PAPER TAPE FORMAT IS THUS LIMITED TO SHORT LOADS OF AT MOST A
/	PORTION OF A SINGLE LOADING FIELD; THE SETTING DETERMINED EXTERNALLY SUCH AS
/	FROM THE CPU FRONT PANEL.

/	WHILE CERTAIN FAIRLY SHORT PROGRAMS ARE KNOWN TO BE PROVIDED IN RIM FORMAT, THE
/	PRIMARY USAGE OF RIM PAPER-TAPE FORMAT IS TO LOAD THE BIN PAPER TAPE LOADER INTO
/	MEMORY USING THE SHORTEST INSTRUCTION COUNT; AS ORIGINALLY DESIGNED, THIS
/	INVOLVES MANUALLY LOADING INTO 07756-07776.  LOCATION 07777 IS NOT USED AS IT IS
/	RESERVED FOR A JMP INSTRUCTION TO THE INTERNAL STARTING ADDRESS OF THE BIN PAPER
/	TAPE LOADER IN USE WHERE RELEVANT.

/	TO MAINTAIN SHORT PROGRAM SIZE, THE RIM PAPER TAPE LOADER WAS DEFINED AS ONE OF
/	TWO VARIANTS, ONE FOR THE ASR CONSOLE READER, AND AN ALTERNATE VERSION OF THE
/	SAME OVERALL LENGTH THAT USES THE HIGH-SPEED READER.  THE BIN LOADER DESIGN MAY
/	BE MORE FLEXIBLE AS THIS LOADER VARIANT IS DESIGNED TO BE READ IN BY PROVIDING
/	THE BIN PAPER TAPE LOADER IN THE READ-IN MODE FORMAT.  AS SUCH, THERE ARE MANY
/	VARIANT LOADERS WITH SLIGHTLY DIFFERENT REQUIREMENTS OR ATTEMPTS TO FIX KNOWN
/	BUTS [BY OCCASIONALLY ADDING ALTERNATE BUGS].

/	THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY CAN PROVIDE A STAND-ALONE COPY OF THE BIN AND RIM PAPER
/	TAPE LOADERS WITH USER OPTIONS CONFIGURING BOTH LOADERS FOR THE REQUESTED
/	HARDWARE CONFGURATION.  IN GENERAL, ALL RIM PAPER TAPE LOADERS ARE IDENTICAL.
/	HOWEVER, THE P?S/8 VARIANT OF THE BIN PAPER TAPE LOADER DOES NOT PROVIDE A
/	DYNAMIC CONFIGURATION FOR THE CHOICE OF INPUT DEVICE.  NO REAL PURPOSE IS SERVED
/	PROVIDING A DEVICE CONFIGURATION CHANGE ONCE STAND-ALONE IN MEMORY; GENERALLY
/	THE FUNCTIONALITY IS PROVIDED BY P?S/8; STAND-ALONE CHOICE VIA THE FRONT-PANEL
/	SWITCH REGISTER IS A SUPERFLUOUS FUNCTION IN THIS SPECIFIC CONTEXT.  MORE
/	IMPORTANTLY, THE CODE SPACE IS REPURPOSED: THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION INCLUDES A
/	BOOTSTRAP TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE AT 07600 ASSUMING THE LOCATIONS FROM 07600-07643
/	ARE NOT VIOLATED BY PAPER-TAPE LOADING. [NOTE: IT IS KNOWN THAT A SMALL NUMBER
/	OF POORLY WRITTEN PROGRAMS VIOLATE A PORTION OF THE SMALL SPACE IN THE RANGE OF
/	07600-07643 OR THEREABOUTS ON THE FALSE ASSUMPTION THESE LOCATIONS ARE SOMEHOW
/	FREELY AVAILABLE.  FOR METHODS OF OVERCOMING THESE LIMITATIONS, SEE
/	DOCUMENTATION ELSEWHERE REGARDING BADLY DESIGNED DEC DIAGNOSTIC PROGRAMS, WHICH
/	FORTUNATELY ARE A MINORITY OF THIS COLLECTION OF PROGRAMS.]








































/, "GET" AND "START" WHICH
/	PERFORMS SEVERAL RELATED FUNCTIONS DEPENDING ON THE EXACT USAGE.  FROM THE
/	OPERATIONAL STANDPOINT, IT IS ACTUALLY THE THREE NAMED PROGRAMS AT ONCE:

/	BIN <OPTIONAL FILES> <OPTION SWITCHES> <OPTIONAL =XXXXX PARAMETER>

/	BIN IS USED TO LOAD BINARY FILES SUCH AS CREATED BY THE P?S PAL ASSEMBLER OR
/	OTHER COMPATIBILE UTILITY.  [NOTE: USED WITH APPROPRIATE OPTION SWITCHES, SUCH
/	FILES CAN BE CREATED BY THE "BIN" UTILITY ITSELF.]


/ [SUCH AS BIN CONVERTING BINARY PAPER TAPES INTO THE
/	CONTENTS OF P?S/8 TFS [TINY FILE SYSTEM] FILES].

/	GET <INPUT FILES> <OPTION SWITCHES>

/	START <OPTIONAL FILES> <OPTION SWITCHES>

/	WHEN INVOKED AS BIN



/	THIS IS THE SHORTEST VERSION OF THE FULLY-COMPATIBLE BIN AND RIM LOADERS TO BE
/	LOADED BY THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY PROGRAM WHEN COMMAND OPTIONS FOR FILES ARE
/	NOT SPECIFIED. [THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY CAN LOAD P?S/8 BINARY FILES INTO
/	MEMORY, OUTPUT P?S/8 BINARY FILES AS PAPER TAPE BINARY IN EITHER BIN OR RIM
/	FORMAT, READ BIN OR RIM BINARY PAPER TAPES AND CONVERT TO P?S/8 BINARY FILES
/	DEPENDING UPON VARIOUS COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES.  BY AVOIDING P?S/8 INPUT
/	AND OUTPUT FILES AND SETTING THE FOLLOWING COMMAND-LINE SWITCHES, BIN AND RIM
/	ARE LOADED INTO MEMORY OVERLAYING THE OPERATING SYSTEM.  HOWEVER, A P?S/8
/	DEVICE-DEPENDENT BOOTSTRAP IS PLACED IN 07600-07642 TO RELOAD P?S/8 BY
/	STARTING AT 07600.]

/	P?S/8 OPTION SWITCHES [WHEN USED WITHOUT INPUT AND OUTPUT FILES] TO INVOKE THE
/	BIN AND RIM LOADERS:

/	/P	LOAD THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS; BY DEFAULT BIN IS STARTED.

/	/R	LOAD THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS; THE RIM LOADER IS STARTED.

/	/F	THE INPUT DEVICE FOR BOTH THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS IS CHANGED TO THE
/		HIGH-SPEED READER.

/	/Z	PRELOAD USER MEMORY [00000-07577 AND X0000-X7777 FOR ANY UNUSED MEMORY
/		FIELD X] WITH 0000.

/	/H	PRELOAD USER MEMORY [00000-07577 AND X0000-X7777 FOR ANY UNUSED MEMORY
/		FIELD X] WITH 7402 [HLT INSTRUCTION].

/	NOTE: SEE P?S/8 MEMORY ALLOCATION DOCUMENTATION FOR THE DEFINITION OF UNUSED
/	EXTENDED MEMORY FIELDS [GENERALLY ALL EXTENDED MEMORY LOCATIONS WITH THE
/	POSSIBLE EXCEPTION OF THE HIGHEST FIELD OF MEMORY AVAILABLE DEPENDING ON P?S/8
/	CONFIGURATION].






