/	COMMENTS:

/	THIS CODE DOES NOT CHECK FOR /0.  IF /1 THROUGH /7 ARE NOT SET, IT IS MERELY
/	IMPLIED.  BETTER CODING SHOULD EXPLICITLY CHECK FOR /0.

/	ONCE THE ABOVE IS IMPLEMENTED, A MASK FOR THE SET BIT CAN BE COMPARED TO THE
/	ENTIRE COLLECTION.  IF MORE THAN ONE BIT IS SET, SIGNAL AN ERROR FOR ANOMALOUS
/	FIELD.  oNE WAY TO DO THIS IS TO FORCE /0 ON IF APPROPRIATE [IF /0 IS EITHER
/	SET OR IMPLIED, FORCE /0 ON].  [NOTE:  IT IS PRESUMED THAT NO OTHER BIN
/	FUNCTIONALIT ACTUALLY CARES ABOUT THIS SUBTLE DISTINCTION.]  THEN INVERT THE
/	BIT BEING CHOSEN TO FORM A MASK FOR THE OTHER SEVEN BITS, AND AGAINST THE ACTUAL
/	/0 THROUGH /7 SWITCHES.  IF NON-ZERO, AT LEAST ONE ADDITIONAL SWITCH IS SET AS
/	AN ANOMALY THAT WILL SIGNAL AN ERROR SUCH AS "MULTIPLE FIELDS SET".] [IN ALL
/	DOCUMENTATION:  "MULTIPLE FIELDS SET" - MORE THAN ONE OPTION SWITCH IN THE
/	RANGE OF /0 THROUGH /7 ARE SET.  ONLY ONE OF THESE IS ALLOWED AT ANY TIME.  IF
/	NONE OF THESE OPTIONS IS SET, /0 APPLIES BY DEFAULT.]


