/	THIS IS THE P?S/8 MODIFIED VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER FOR STANDALONE USAGE
/	[SUCH AS RUNNING DIAGNOSTIC PROGRAMS ON BINARY PAPER TAPES] AND THE RIM LOADER
/	[WHICH IS ESSENTIALLY UNMODIFIED FROM THE DEC ORIGINAL CODE].  THE BIN LOADER
/	HAS BEEN MADE TO OCCUPY THE SHORTEST OVERALL CODE SPACE BY THE USE OF VARIOUS
/	OPTIMIZATION TECHNIQUES.

/	BIN LOADER START AT 07777.

/	THIS FEATURE HAS BEEN RETAINED FOR FULL COMPATIBILITY.  THERE ARE ACTUALLY
/	SEVERAL DIFFERENT IMPLEMENTATIONS OF WHAT IS COMMONLY REFERRED TO AS THE BIN
/	LOADER AS DEC [AND OTHERS] HAVE MADE CHANGES TO THIS CLASS OF PROGRAM OVER THE
/	YEARS.  INSTEAD OF DOCUMENTING THE INTERNAL STARTING ADDRESS, LOCATION 07777
/	CONTAINS A "JMP BEGIN" INSTRUCTION SPECIFIC TO THIS IMPLEMENTATION.

/	DYNAMIC CHOICE OF LOW-SPEED OR HIGH-SPEED READER.

/	IN MOST OF THE DEC VERSIONS OF THE BIN LOADER, THE CHOICE OF INPUT DEVICE IS
/	DETERMINED ON THE FRONT PANEL OF THE COMPUTER USING THE HIGH-ORDER BIT OF THE
/	CONSOLE SWITCH REGISTER.  IN THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION, THIS IS CHOSEN BY
/	SETTING PROPER COMMAND LINE OPTIONS WHEN INVOKING THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY
/	[WHICH IS USED FOR SEVERAL OTHER MODES OF OPERATION SUCH AS THE LOADING OF
/	P?S/8 BINARY FILES INTO MEMORY].  ASSUMING PROPER COMMAND-LINE PARTICULARS TO
/	INVOKE THE LOW-SPEED VERSION OF THE RIM AND BIN LOADERS, ADDING /F TO THE SAME
/	COMMAND CAUSES THE PROGRAM TO USE THE HIGH-SPEED READER HARDWARE FOR ALL READ
/	FUNCTIONS.  AS NECESSARY, COMMENTS ARE PROVIDED BELOW TO INDICATE THE ALTERED
/	CONTENTS OF ALL MEMORY LOCATIONS AFFECTED BY THE USE OF THE HIGH-SPEED READER.

/	RUBOUT PROTECTION SUPPORT.

/	AS OF THIS WRITING, THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER SUPPORTS THE OBSCURE
/	FEATURE OF IGNORING IMBEDDED ERROR MESSAGES WITHIN BINARY PAPER TAPES WHEN
/	PRECEDED AND FOLLOWED BY <RO> [CODE 377] CHARACTERS.  VIRTUALLY ALL RELEASED
/	VERSIONS OF BIN FORMAT BINARY PAPER TAPES DO NOT REQUIRE THIS FEATURE; IT IS
/	ONLY POSSIBLE WHEN INCOMPLETELY DEVELOPED PROGRAMS [THAT STILL HAVE DETECTED
/	ASSEMBLY ERRORS] ARE BEING LOADED [PRESUMABLY FOR DEBUGGING PURPOSES] AND ONLY
/	IF PUNCHED ON THE CONSOLE TELETYPE PUNCH USING PROGRAMS SUCH AS THE PAPER TAPE
/	VERSION OF PAL III. [NOTE: IF THE HIGH-SPEED PUNCH IS USED TO CREATE THE
/	BINARY PAPER TAPES, ERROR MESSAGES ARE STILL ISSUED TO THE CONSOLE TERMINAL.
/	AS SUCH, THE PROBLEMATIC CIRCUMSTANCES BEING ADDRESSED CANNOT OCCUR.]
/	FOR THE VAST MAJORITY OF USERS, THIS FEATURE IS TRULY MEANINGLESS.  AS SUCH,
/	FUTURE RELEASES OF THE P?S/8 "BIN" PROGRAM MAY DROP SUPPORT OF THIS FEATURE IN
/	FAVOR OF SUPPORT OF LONGER REBOOT CODE AND/OR GREATER PROGRAM RELIABILITY.
/	SHOULD LOADING OF PROBLEMATIC PAPER TAPES BE REQUIRED, THE DEC STANDARD BIN
/	LOADER CAN BE LOADED BY THE RIM LOADER.  HOWEVER, THE P?S/8 RESTART AT 07600
/	WILL BE DESTROYED REQUIRING MANUAL ENTRY OF SPECIFIC BOOTSTRAP CODE FOR THE
/	P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE HARDWARE. [NOTE: THE CURRENT RELEASE OF THE P?S/8 "BIN"
/	UTILITY CAN CREATE P?S/8 BINARY FILES FROM BINARY PAPER TAPE INPUT IN EITHER
/	BIN OR RIM FORMAT USING APPROPRIATE COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS.  P?S/8 "BIN" CAN
/	ALSO BE USED WITH OTHER COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS TO PUNCH BINARY PAPER TAPES FROM
/	THE CONTENTS OF P?S/8 BINARY FILES ON THE SYSTEM DEVICE.  AS SUCH, P?S/8 CAN
/	BE USED TO NOT ONLY STORE ANY PROBLEMATIC BINARY DATA, BUT TO ALSO CREATE A
/	DESCENDENT BINARY PAPER TAPE WITHOUT THE PROBLEMATIC ERROR MESSAGES; THE
/	RESULTANT PAPER TAPE WOULD BE SOMEWHAT SHORTER WITH THE ERROR MESSAGE TEXT
/	REMOVED.]
/	
/	BY MINIMIZING THE CODE SPACE OCCUPIED BY THE BIN LOADER TO 07643-07755 [WHICH
/	IS ADJACENT TO THE RIM LOADER THAT OCCUPIES 07756-07776], A P?S/8 BOOTSTRAP
/	CAN BE LOADED INTO 07600-07642.  P?S/8 IS NOT LOADED INTO MEMORY WHEN THE BIN
/	AND RIM LOADERS ARE PRESENT, BUT RESTARTING AT 07600 WILL ALLOW P?S/8 TO BE
/	REBOOTED WITHOUT MANAL ENTRY OF A TOGGLE-IN BOOTSTRAP.  [NOTE: MOST DEVICES
/	SPECIFY A SMALL BOOTSTRAP ROUTINE TO RELOAD THE OPERATING SYSTEM, BUT THERE IS
/	NO CONSISTENCY AS TO THE PROGRAM ADDRESSES OR EXACT OPERATIONAL STEPS USED TO
/	PERFORM THE BOOTUP OPERATION.  BY PROVIDING A STANDARD RELOAD ROUTINE AT THE
/	UNIVERSAL EXIT LOCATION OF 07600, P?S/8 CAN MANAGE THE SYSTEM IN THE OVERALL
/	SENSE.  THIS CONCEPT IS UNIQUE TO P?S/8 AND ITS PREDECESSOR, THE R-L MONITOR
/	SYSTEM.  HOWEVER, THE R-L MONITOR SYSTEM ONLY SUPPORTS SYSTEM RESTART AT 07600
/	FOM THE "SLURP" LOADER FOR BINARY FILES WHILE P?S/8 USES THE SAME BOOTSTRAP
/	CODE WITH THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS AS WELL.]

/	ANY DECISION TO DROP SUPPORT OF THE<RO>-ENCLOSED ERROR MESSAGES WILL BE BASED
/	ON THE NEED TO SUPPORT P?S/8 RESTART CODE AT 07600 FOR FUTURE DEVICES.  ALL
/	CURRENTLY SUPPORTED CONFIGURATIONS CAN BE SUCCESSFULLY IMPLEMENTED WITHIN
/	07600-07642. [NOTE: P?S/8 EXTENDED SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLERS REQUIRE ADDITIONAL
/	MEMORY FOR THIS FUNCTION; HOWEVER, ALL ADDITIONAL CODING RESIDES IN EXTENDED
/	MEMORY PRIMARILY IN SUPPORT OF A "SLURP" LOADER FOR THE DEVICE.

/	POTENTIAL BIN LOADER CORRUPTION BY THREE-CYCLE DATA BREAK DEVICES.

/	ALL VERSIONS OF THE BIN LOADER CAN BE DESTROYED BY OPERATION OF CERTAIN
/	THREE-CYCLE DATA BREAK DEVICES [DF32/RF08, TC58 MAGNETIC TAPE, TC01/TC08
/	DECTAPE.  EACH VERSION HAS DIFFERENT LIMITATIONS; THE DEC BINARY LOADER
/	DEC-08-LBAA, RELEASED MAY 10, 1967, WILL BE PARTIALLY DESTROYED BY THE USE OF
/	THE RF08 OR DF32 DISKS.  THE ONLY LIMITATION IN THE P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION OF
/	THE BIN LOADER IS INTERACTION WITH THE TC58 MAGNETIC TAPE CONTROLLER.  THE
/	PROBLEM CAN BE REMEDIED BY LOADING A FRESH COPY OF THE BIN LOADER USING THE
/	RIM LOADER OR RESTARTING P?S/8 [HOPEFULLY AT 07600]. [NOTE: BY ELIMINATING THE
/	RUBOUT PROTECTION FEATURE, THE PROBLEM CAN BE ELIMINATED [AS WELL AS ALLOWING
/	THE P?S/8 RESTART CODE TO BE SOMEWHAT LONGER.]
	IFNZRO	BINSTRT-.	<ERROR	.>	/ENSURE PROPER LOADING ADDRESS.

/	"BEGG" SUBROUTINE; EXTRACT ERRORS, FIELD SETTINGS, LEADER/TRAILER.

/	"BEGG" OPERATES IN A DATA-DEPENDENT MANNER AFTER FIRST OBTAINING A DATA FRAME
/	FROM THE PAPER TAPE READER:

/	1) THE LATEST FRAME IS A LEADER/TRAILER CODE OF THE FORM "2XY" WHERE "XY" IS
/	   IGNORED.  TAKE NON-SKIP RETURN TO CALLER; THE CALLER DETERMINES WHAT TO DO
/	   WHEN LEADER/TRAILER FRAMES ARE DETECTED. [NOTE: LEADER/TRAILER FRAMES DO
/	   NOT CONTRIBUTE TO THE OVERALL CHECKSUM CALCULATION.]

/	2) THE LATEST FRAME IS A FIELD SETTING TO FIELD X OF THE FORM "3XY" WHERE "Y"
/	   IS IGNORED.  FORM A "CDF X0" INSTRUCTION AND STORE FOR LATER USE.  CONTINUE
/	   PROCESSING BY OBTAINING AN ADDITIONAL DATA FRAME. [NOTE: FIELD SETTINGS DO
/	   NOT CONTRIBUTE TO THE OVERALL CHECKSUM CALCULATION.]

/	3) THE LATEST FRAME IS THE FIRST HALF OF EITHER AN ORIGIN SETTING OF THE FORM
/	   "01AB" WHERE THE COMPLETE ORIGIN WILL BE USED TO UPDATE THE STORAGE POINTER
/	   TO MEMORY LOCATION "ABCD", OR A DATA WORD OF THE FORM "00AB" WHERE THE
/	   COMPLETE DATA WILL BE "ABCD".  TAKE SKIP RETURN TO CALLER. [NOTE: THE
/	   SECOND HALF OF THE LATEST ORIGIN OR DATA ["CD"] IS OBTAINED BY THE CALLER
/	   AS NECESSARY.] THE ENTIRE DATA FRAME CONTRIBUTES TO THE OVERALL CHECKSUM
/	   CALCULATION INCLUDING BIT[5] WHICH IS SET FOR THE FIRST HALF OF AN ORIGIN
/	   SETTING; SECOND HALF DATA FRAMES ARE ALWAYS OF THE FORM "0CD". [NOTE:
/	   BINARY PAPER TAPES CREATED WITH "DTORG" STATEMENTS ARE INCOMPATIBLE WITH
/	   THE BIN LOADER AND MUST BE PROCESSED BY ALTERNATE PROGRAMMING SUCH AS A
/	   SPECIAL LOADING PROGRAM CREATED BY THE TYPESET-8 GROUP.]

BEGG,	.-.				/GET A NEW FILTERED FRAME ROUTINE.
BEGG1,	JMS	READ			/GET A CHARACTER.
	TAD	M376/(-376)		/TEST FOR 377.
	SPA SNA CLA			/SKIP IF <RO> CODE.
SWINST,	JMP	NOTRUB			/**** <RO> CODE NOT FOUND YET **** JMP NOTRUB
					/**** <RO> CODE FOUND PREVIOUSLY **** JMP BEGG1

/	<RO> DETECTED.  REVERSE THE STATE OF <RO> HANDLING.

	TAD	SWINST			/GET THE PRESENT INSTRUCTION VALUE.
	CIA				/INVERT IT.
	TAD	FLIPIT			/ADD ON INSTRUCTION SUM YIELDING THE OTHER ONE.
	DCA	SWINST			/STORE INLINE.
	JMP	BEGG1			/GO GET ANOTHER FRAME.

/	REVERSING <RO> HANDLING MODE.

/	IF A <RO> CODE HASN'T OCCURRED BEFORE, ALL CHARACTERS THAT FOLLOW MUST BE
/	IGNORED.  WHEN A SECOND <RO> CODE OCCURS, THE IGNORED SECTION IS COMPLETE;
/	NORMAL CHARACTER DETECTION WILL BE RESTORED.

/	LOCATION "SWINST" CAN CONTAIN EITHER OF TWO VALUES ["JMP NOTRUB", "JMP BEGG1"]
/	DEPENDING ON THE STATE OF <RO> CHARACTER DETECTION.
/	COMES HERE IF NO <RO> CONSIDERATION.

NOTRUB,	TAD	CHAR			/GET LATEST CHARACTER.
	AND	MASK/(300)		/JUST CONTROLLING BITS.
	TAD	M200/(-200)		/COMPARE TO LEADER/TRAILER CODE.
	SPA				/SKIP IF LEADER/TRAILER CODE OR FIELD SETTING.
	ISZ	BEGG			/TAKE SKIP RETURN ON DATA OR ORIGIN SETTING.
	SPA SNA CLA			/SKIP IF FIELD SETTING.
	JMP I	BEGG			/TAKE IMMEDIATE RETURN ON LEADER/TRAILER CODE.

/	FIELD SETTING FOUND.

	TAD	CHAR			/GET LATEST CHARACTER.
MASK,	AND	FMASK/(70)		/JUST FIELD BITS.
	TAD	CHANGE/(CDF 00)		/FORM "CDF" INSTRUCTION TO LATEST FIELD.
	DCA	MEMTEM			/SAVE FOR FURTHER LOADING.
	JMP	BEGG1			/GO GET ANOTHER FRAME.

READ,	.-.				/READ A CHARACTER ROUTINE.
READ1,	KSF				/FLAG UP? **** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RSF
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
READ3,	KRB				/YES, READ IT IN.
					/**** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RFC RRB
	DCA	CHAR			/SAVE LATEST CHARACTER.
	TAD	CHAR			/GET IT BACK.
	JMP I	READ			/RETURN TO CALLER.

	IFNZRO	.&177-100	<ERROR	.>

FMASK,	70				/FIELD MASK CONSTANT 0070
CHANGE,	CDF	00			/"CDF 00" INSTRUCTION CONSTANT 6201

/	TRAILER CODE SEEN.

BEND,	JMS	ASSEMB			/ASSEMBLE CHECKSUM FROM THE TAPE.
	CIA				/INVERT.
	TAD	CHKSUM			/SUBTRACT ACCUMULATED CHECKSUM.
M376,	HLT				/HALT AT END OF LOADING.  IF AC IS CLEAR,
					/APPARENTLY THE TAPE LOADED WITHOUT ERRORS.
					/ALSO USED AS CONSTANT -376.

/	PRESS CONTINUE TO LOAD ANOTHER BIN PAPER TAPE.  THIS IS THE STARTING ADDRESS
/	OF THE BIN LOADER.  A "JMP BEGIN" INSTRUCTION IS PLACED INTO 07777 AS THE
/	OFFICIAL DOCUMENTED STARTING ADDRESS.

BEGIN,	KCC				/CLEAR THE KEYBOARD FLAG TO START THE READER.
					/**** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RFC
M200,	CLA!400				/CLEAN UP; ALSO FORMS CONSTANT 7600.
	RDF				/GET CURRENT DATA FIELD.
	TAD	CHANGE/(CDF 00)		/CREATE "CDF" INSTRUCTION TO CURRENT DATA FIELD.
	DCA	MEMTEM			/SAVE FOR LOADING DATA.
	JMS	BEGG			/GET A NEW CHARACTER.
	JMP	.-1			/LEADER FOUND, IGNORE AND TRY AGAIN.
GO,	DCA	CHKSUM			/STORE NEW CHECKSUM VALUE.
	TAD	MEMTEM			/GET "CDF" TO LATEST DATA FIELD.
	DCA	MEMFLD			/STORE IN-LINE.
	TAD	CHAR			/GET THE LATEST CHARACTER.
	DCA	WORD1			/SAVE IT.
	JMS	READ			/GET THE SECOND CHARACTER.
	DCA	WORD2			/SAVE IT.
	JMS	BEGG			/LOOK AHEAD FOR THE NEXT CHARACTER.
	JMP	BEND			/TRAILER CODE FOUND.
	JMS	ASSEMB			/ASSEMBLE LATEST WORD.
MEMFLD,	HLT				/WILL BE "CDF" TO LATEST DATA FIELD.
	SNL				/SKIP IF ORIGIN SETTING.
	DCA I	TEMP			/STORE DATA WORD.
	ISZ	TEMP			/BUMP TO NEXT LOCATION.
	SZL				/SKIP IF DATA AND NOT AT LOCATION 0000.
	DCA	TEMP			/STORE NEW ORIGIN SETTING [POSSIBLY 0000].
CHEX,	TAD	WORD1			/GET LATEST FIRST CHARACTER.
	TAD	WORD2			/GET LATEST SECOND CHARACTER
	TAD	CHKSUM			/ADD ON RUNNING CHECKSUM
	JMP	GO			/KEEP GOING.

ASSEMB,	.-.				/WORD ASSEMBLE ROUTINE.
	TAD	WORD1			/GET FIRST CHARACTER.
	CLL RTL;RTL;RTL			/MOVE UP.
	TAD	WORD2			/ADD SECOND CHARACTER.
	JMP I	ASSEMB			/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	IMPLEMENTATION NOTES:

/	THE DEC BIN LOADER PROGRAM EVOLVED OVER SEVERAL GENERATIONS OF DEVELOPMENT.
/	IT IS APPARENT THAT EXTENDED MEMORY LOADING AND OTHER CONSIDERATIONS CAUSED
/	INCREMENTAL CHANGES TO THE CODING THAT IN HINDSIGHT WAS NOT WELL ORGANIZED.
/	[AND LIKELY THERE WAS LITTLE IMPETUS TO MODIFY THE CODE OTHER THAN TO REPAIR
/	PROBLEMS AS THEY UNFOLDED.]  P?S/8 ADDS THE ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENT OF USING
/	MORE EFFICIENT CODING TECHNIQUES TO ACHIEVE A SMALLER OVERALL CODE SPACE
/	TO MAXIMIZE THE SIZE OF A SYSTEM REBOOT SEQUENCE THAT LOADS INTO 07600 AND THE
/	FOLLOWING LOCATIONS WHILE THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS OCCUPY THE REST OF THE LAST
/	PAGE OF FIELD 0.

/	AS SUCH, CERTAIN SLOPPY "SPAGHETTI CODE" SEQUENCES HAVE BEEN REPLACED BY A
/	MORE COHERENT SECTION THAT IS ACTUALLY MORE STRAIGHTFORWARD THAN THE ORIGINAL
/	CODE. [NOTE: THE P?S/8 REPLACEMENT CODE DEPENDS ON QUIRKS OF THE PDP-8
/	INSTRUCTION SET CLEARLY NOT FULLY UNDERSTOOD BY THE ORIGINAL PROGRAMMERS OF
/	THE BIN LOADER.  THOSE INTERESTED IN SEEING HOW THE ORIGINAL CODING WAS
/	REWORKED ARE REFERRED TO THE DOCUMENTATION OF THE BINARY LOADER DEC-08-LBAA-D,
/	MAY 10, 1967.]
/	SELF-REFERENTIAL CODING TECHNIQUES.

/	THE ORIGINAL VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER USES THE VALID PROGRAMMING TECHNIQUE
/	OF CONTRIVING INSTRUCTIONS THAT FORM USEFUL CONSTANTS.  FOR EXAMPLE, THERE IS
/	A NEED TO COMPARE THE LATEST PAPER TAPE FRAME TO 377.  AN INITIAL DESIGN PASS
/	MIGHT START BY COMPARING THE LATEST CHARACTER TO 377 BY INVERTING THE LATEST
/	CHARACTER AND ADDING THE CONSTANT 0377, THEN CHECK FOR A ZERO ACCUMULATOR.  AN
/	OBVIOUS OPTIMIZATION IS TO INSTEAD COMPARE THE CHARACTER TO THE CONSTANT -377
/	WHICH SAVES ONE WORD.  HOWEVER, THE BIN LOADER INCLUDES THE HLT INSTRUCTION
/	[7402] WHICH IS ALSO THE SIGNED CONSTANT -376.  BY CHANGING THE COMPARISON TO
/	SKIP ON STRICTLY POSITIVE, ALL CODES LESS THAN 377 ARE SEPARATED FROM THE
/	DETECTION OF THE 377 CODE ACCOMPLISHING SUFFICIENTLY SIMILAR LOGIC WHILE ALSO
/	SAVING AN OVERALL MEMORY LOCATION.  SIMILARLY, ANOTHER INSTRUCTION THAT IS
/	NEEDED TO CLEAR THE ACCUMULATOR ["CLA" IS NORMALLY DEFINED AS THE GROUP I
/	INSTRUCTION 7200] IS CONTRIVED INTO THE CONSTANT 7600 BY INSTEAD USING THE
/	GROUP II INSTRUCTION TO CLEAR THE ACCUMULATOR.  THIS TECHNIQUE ALSO SAVES A
/	MEMORY LOCATION.

/	THE P?S/8 MODIFICATIONS TAKE THIS CONCEPT ANOTHER STEP FURTHER.  THE BIN
/	LOADER CODING REQUIRES A CONSTANT 0300 AND A CONSTANT 0070.  BY REQUIRING THE
/	"FMASK" CONSTANT [0070] TO BE LOCATED AT LOCATION 7700 WITHIN THE LOADER, THE
/	LOCATION THAT REFERENCES THE CONSTANT, THE INSTRUCTION "AND FMASK", CAN BE
/	ITSELF USED AS THE CONSTANT 0300 WITHOUT REQUIRING AN ADDITIONAL MEMORY
/	LOCATION.  IN THEORY, ADDITIONAL TECHNIQUES COULD BE DISCOVERED IN THE FUTURE.

/	EXTENDED MEMORY CONSIDERATIONS OF BIN FORMAT PAPER TAPES.

/	DUE TO THE WAY THE BIN LOADER DETECTS FIELD SETTINGS [IGNORING THEM FOR
/	CHECKSUM PURPOSES] A "CDF <NEW DATA FIELD" INSTRUCTION IS CREATED AND BUFFERED
/	FOR USE WITH LATER DATA TO BE LOADED.  A DEFECTIVE VERSION OF DEC'S BIN LOADER
/	WAS RELEASED KNOWN AS THE "SELF-STARTING BINARY LOADER".  THIS RELEASE IS
/	FLAWED AS IT LACKS THE REQUIRED BUFFERING; IT WAS APPARENTLY WRITTEN BY
/	SOMEONE IGNORANT OF THE NUANCES OF BINARY PAPER-TAPE FORMAT AS IT APPLIES TO
/	LOADING INTO EXTENDED MEMORY.

/	THE ONLY REASON THIS SERIOUS PROBLEM WAS NOT DETECTED UNTIL POST-RELEASE IS
/	THAT MOST FIELD SETTINGS IN PRACTICAL PDP-8 CODE ARE FOLLOWED BY AN ORIGIN
/	SETTING; THE PREMATURE FIELD CHANGE DOESN'T AFFECT ORIGIN SETTINGS.  HOWEVER,
/	THERE IS NO RULE REGARDING THIS CIRCUMSTANCE; CERTAIN PAL ASSEMBLERS CAN BE
/	USED SUCH THAT THERE IS NO "PROTECTIVE" ORIGIN SETTING FOLLOWING FIELD
/	SETTINGS.  THIS RELEASE OF THE BINARY LOADER HONORS THE ORIGINAL PAPER TAPE
/	CONTENTS COMPLETELY AND CORRECTLY.

/	THREE-CYCLE DATA BREAK CONSIDERATIONS.

/	THE RIM LOADER IS NOT AFFECTED BY RUNNING PROGRAMS THAT USE THE THREE CYCLE
/	DATA BREAK LOCATIONS ASSIGNED AS FOLLOWS:

/	07750-07751	DF32/RF08

/	07752-07753	TC58 MAGNETIC TAPE

/	07754-07755	TC01/TC08 DECTAPE
CHAR,	.-.				/BUFFER FOR LATEST CHARACTER FRAME.
MEMTEM,	.-.				/WILL CONTAIN "CDF" TO LATEST DATA FIELD.
CHKSUM,	.-.				/CHECKSUM ACCUMULATION TEMPORARY.

/	<RO> STATE REVERSAL CONSTANT.

/	LOCATION "FLIPIT" CONTAINS THE SUM OF THE TWO POSSIBLE VALUES ["JMP BEGG1" AND
/	"JMP NOTRUB"] TO ENABLE FLIPPING BETWEEN THE TWO INSTRUCTIONS STORED IN
/	"SWINST" AS REQUIRED.  THE CURRENT CONTENTS OF "SWINST" WILL BE SUBTRACTED
/	FROM THE CONTENTS OF "FLIPIT" WHICH WILL THEN BE STORED IN "SWINST" REPLACING
/	THE CONTENTS WITH THE OTHER INSTRUCTION.

	INST1=	JMP	NOTRUB		/FIRST POSSIBLE VALUE OF SWINST.

	INST2=	JMP	BEGG1		/SECOND POSSIBLE VALUE OF SWINST.

FLIPIT,	INST1+INST2			/SUM OF BOTH POSSIBLE VALUES.

WORD1,	.-.				/FIRST CHARACTER.
WORD2,	JMS I	41/.-.			/SECOND CHARACTER.
					/NOTE: MODIFED FOR SPECIAL P?S/8 RIM LOADER
					/MODIFICATIONS WHEN INTERCEPTING RIM INPUT.
					
/	STAND-ALONE PAPER-TAPE RIM LOADER STARTS HERE.

BEG,	KCC				/CLEAR THE KEYBOARD FLAG, START THE READER.
					/**** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RFC
BEG1,	KSF				/FLAG UP? **** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RSF
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
BEG3,	KRB				/YES, READ IT LATEST AND START ANOTHER.
					/**** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RFC RRB
	CLL RTL;RTL			/MOVE LEADER/TRAILER BIT TO AC[0]
	SPA				/SKIP IF NOT LEADER CODE.
	JMP	CLRAC			/FOUND LEADER, IGNORE IT.
	RTL				/MOVE FIRST HALF TO HIGH-ORDER BITS.
BEG11,	KSF				/FLAG UP? **** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RSF
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
BEG13,	KRS				/YES, READ IT IN.
					/**** HIGH-SPEED READER **** RRB
	SNL				/SKIP IF ORIGIN SETTING.
	DCA I	TEMP			/STORE LATEST DATA WORD.
CLRAC,	DCA	TEMP			/STORE LATEST ORIGIN.
	JMP	BEG			/KEEP GOING.

TEMP,	.-.				/STORAGE ORIGIN TEMPORARY.

/	OFFICIAL STARTING ADDRESS FOR ALL VERSIONS OF THE BIN LOADER.

/	WITH SO MANY IMPLEMENTATIONS OF THE BIN LOADER, DEC WISELY DOCUMENTED THIS
/	OFFICIAL STARTING ADDRESS OF 07777, WHICH IS ACTUALLY A "JMP" INSTRUCTION TO
/	THE INTERNAL STARTING ADDRESS REGARDLESS OF IMPLEMENTATION.

	JMP	BEGIN			/START BIN LOADER AT OFFICIAL START ADDRESS.

/	P?S/8 RIM LOADER CONSIDERATIONS.

/	THE P?S/8 RIM LOADER IS NOT 100% IDENTICAL TO THE DEC VERSION DEFINED IN
/	DEC-08-LRAA-D, FEBRUARY 23, 1965.  MODIFICATIONS HAVE BEEN MADE TO SIMPLFY
/	SUPPORT FOR THE HIGH-SPEED READER.

/	1) THE OFFICIAL LOW-SPEED RIM LOADER USES THE "KRB" INSTRUCTION TO READ IN
/	   POTENTIAL LEADER FRAMES.  AS SUCH, WHEN IGNORING THE INPUT, THE PROGRAM
/	   LOOPS BACK TO "BEG1" SINCE THE "KRB" INSTRUCTION HAS ALREADY STARTED THE
/	   READER FOR THE NEXT CHARACTER.

/	2) THE OFFICIAL HIGH-SPEED RIM LOADER USES THE "RFC RRB" COMBINED INSTRUCTION
/	   IN THE SAME CODE POSITION.  WHEN IGNORING THE INPUT, THE PROGRAM JUMPS TO
/	   "CLRAC" TO CLEAR THE AC, AND THEN JUMPS TO "BEG1".

/	3) THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE LOW-SPEED RIM LOADER USES THE SAME INSTRUCTION AS
/	   THE HIGH-SPEED VERSION THUS USES "CLRAC" TO ACCOMPLISH THE SAME RESULT.
/	   HOWEVER, THE ULTIMATE JUMP IS TO "BEG" AND NOT "BEG1".

/	   DUE TO THE WAY THE LOW-SPEED TELETYPE READER MECHANISM FUNCTIONS, IT IS
/	   COMPLETELY SAFE TO START THE READER SEVERAL TIMES WITHIN THE FIRST FEW
/	   MICROSECONDS ONCE INITIATED.  SINCE THE RIM LOADER CAN BE STARTED MANUALLY,
/	   THE READER WILL BE STARTED BOTH BY THE CPU POWER CLEAR AND THE KCC
/	   INSTRUCTION THAT STARTS THE PROGRAM.

/	4) ASSUMING THE JUMP IN THE "CLRAC" PORTION IS TO "BEG" AND NOT "BEG1", THE
/	   HIGH-SPEED RIM LOADER WILL START THE READER TWICE.  IT APPEARS THAT THE
/	   SAME CONSIDERATION APPLIES; STARTING THE READER MORE THAN ONCE WITHIN THE
/	   FIRST FEW MICROSECONDS OF THE FIRST INITIATION IS HARMLESS.

/	   FOR FULL AUTHENTICITY, FUTURE RELEASES OF THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY WILL
/	   CHANGE THE PARTICULARS SUCH THAT THE AUTHENTIC VERSIONS OF BOTH THE LOW AND
/	   HIGH-SPEED RIM LOADERS WILL BE SUPPORTED.  [NOTE: AS OF THIS WRITING, THIS
/	   SOURCE CODE IS BASED ON THE 1978 RELEASE OF P?S/8.]

	RELOC				/TURN OFF RELOCATION.


