/	ABORT CHARACTER CHECK ROUTINE.

/	AS ORIGINALLY WRITTEN, CHECKS FOR A KEYBOARD ABORT CODE BY THE PRIMITIVE MEANS
/	OF COMPARING THE LATEST CHARACTER CODE TO 7774.  IF LESS THAN 0004, TAKE ABORT
/	EXIT TO 07600.

/	THIS NEEDS TO BE MODERNIZED IN SEVERAL WAYS:

/	1) CHANGE TO ONLY ABORT ON <CTRL-C> OR <CTRL-B> ONLY.

/	2) CHANGE THE CODE TO THE DECMATE-COMPATIBLE MECHANISM OF USING KRB IF IT IS
/	   DISCOVERED THE PROGRAM IS OPERATING ON A 6120.  AND IF SO, CHANGE TO ALLOW
/	   THE SOFT ABORT STATUS TO BE SET.  THE CURRENT METHOD IS ACCEPTABLE ONLY ON A
/	   PDP-8 MODEL.  THIS WAS LIKELY DONE SOME YEARS AFER THIS CODE WAS ORIGINALLY
/	   WRITTEN.  NOTE:  BY NATURE, DECMATES HAVE VIRTUALLY NO NEED FOR ANY UTILITIES
/	   ORIENTED AROUND PAPER-TAPE; USEFUL OPERATIONS WILL INVOLVE LITTLE MORE THAN
/	   LOADING BINARY FILES.

ABRTCHK,.-.				/ABORT CHECK ROUTINE.
	KSF				/FLAG UP?
	JMP I	ABRTCHK			/NO, JUST RETURN.
	KRS				/YES, READ THE CHARACTER; DON'T DISTURB FLAG.
	AND	ZZ1566/(177)		/JUST SEVEN-BITS.
	TAD	ZZ1575/(-4)		/CHECK IF <CTRL-C> OR LESS.
	SMA CLA				/SKIP IF LESS THAN <CTRL-D>.
	JMP I	ABRTCHK			/RETURN ON NON-ABORT CHARACTER DETECTED.

