/	THE PROGRAM IS ENTERED HERE IF INVOKED AS "GET".

/	THE GET COMMAND IS IDENTICAL TO THE BIN COMMAND EXCEPT CERTAIN PARAMETERS ARE
/	PRESET:

/	1) =7632 IS FORCED TO ENSURE THE STARTING ADDRESS IS THAT OF THE SYSTEM LOADER
/	   WHICH WILL BE PRELOADED WITH A CALL TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER TO SAVE
/	   ALL OF FIELD 0 INTO BLOCKS 0020-0057 AND THEN REBOOT. [NOTE: ALL SYSTEM
/	   DEVICES THAT SUPPORT THE /I SWITCH IMPLEMENTING THE RELOADING OF THE SYSTEM
/	   DEVICE HANDLER ARE REQUIRED TO PRELOAD THE SYSTEM LOADER WITH THE PROPER
/	   ARGUMENTS.]

/	2) THE /G SWITCH IS FORCED ON TO ENSURE IT IS UNDERSTOOD THIS USAGE OF THE BIN
/	   UTILITY IS TO LOAD BINARY FILES AS OPPOSED TO ANY PAPER TAPE OPERATION WHEN
/	   LOADING ACTUALLY OCCURS.  THIS ALLOWS THE REMOTE POSSIBILITY OF CREATING
/	   BINARY OUTPUT FILES FROM PAPER TAPE INPUT, THEN CHAINING BACK TO BIN FOR
/	   THE PURPOSE OF ALSO LOADING THE FILES, SAVING ALL OF FIELD 0 AND THEN
/	   REBOOTING.  NOTE: THIS MECHANISM IS SUBJECT TO ITS OWN RULES; HOWEVER, IT
/	   IS THEORETICALLY POSSIBLE.

/	3) THE /I SWITCH IS FORCED ON TO INCLUDE THE SLURP LOADER RELOAD ROUTINE
/	   [CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0060 ON THE SAME SYSTEM DEVICE UNIT BIN IS LOCATED ON]
/	   AT THE END OF THE INPUT FILE LIST TO CAUSE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER TO BE
/	   RELOADED.  NOTE: THIS IS MOOT IF THE /V SWITCH IS PASSED [OR THE DEFAULT
/	   LOADER IS THE VIRTUAL LOADER ON THIS SYSTEM].

	TAD I	PSWAL/[SWAL]		/GET /A-/L SWITCHES.
	AND	L7727/(7727)		/REMOVE /G, /I SWITCHES.
	TAD	L50/(50)		/FORCE /G, /I SWITCHES ON.
	DCA I	PSWAL/[SWAL]		/STORE BACK TO BE READ LATER.
	TAD I	PSWY9/[SWY9]		/GET /Y-/9 SWITCHES.
	AND	O7000/[7000]		/JUST KEEP /Y, /Z, /0 SWITCHES.
	DCA I	PSWY9/[SWY9]		/STORE BACK.
	TAD	ZZ0023/[SLOAD]		/GET ADDRESS OF THE SYSTEM LOADER.
	DCA I	ZZ0044/[SEQUALS]	/FORCE =7632.

/	NOTE:  IT IS NOT CLEAR WHAT THE /Y SWITCH DOES!

/	THE CODE FALLS INTO THE ENTRY POINT FOR "BIN".

/	COMMENTS:

/	THIS CODE IS ESSENTIALLY FUNCTIONAL.  HOWEVER, THERE ARE A FEW THEORETICAL
/	CONSIDERATIONS:

/	1) THE /0 SWITCH IS MERELY BEING ALLOWED.  IT OUGHT TO BE FORCED TO BE 100%
/	   CERTAIN IT IS SET.  THE DOCUMENTATION SHOULD BE UPGRADED TO INDICATE THIS
/	   TO AVOID THE NEEDLESS EXPLANATION REGARDING THE /0 SWITCH BEING IMPLIED IF
/	   NONE OF THE SWITCHES IN THE RANGE OF /0 THROUGH /7 IS ACTUALY SET WHEN
/	   USING THE "GET" COMMAND [OR ANY SIMILAR CONTEXT].  IT IS CONCEIVABLE THIS
/	   CODE SHOULD BE MADE MORE GENERIC AND ALSO BE PART OF CODE TO CHECK FOR THE
/	   ANOMALY OF TWO OR MORE OF THESE SWITCHES SET AT THE SAME TIME. [ANY ONE
/	   SWITCH IN THE RANGE OF /0 THROUGH /7 IS SET AS PASSED; IF NO SWITCH IS SET
/	   THE /0 SWITCH WILL BE SET TO INDICATE THE DEFAULT TO FIELD 0.  MORE THAN
/	   ONE SWITCH IN THE RANGE OF /0 THROUGH /7 WILL YIELD A FATAL ERROR MESSAGE
/	   AND A FORCED EXIT.

/	2) CLEARLY THERE IS A NEED TO REMOVE THE /1 THROUGH /7 SWITCHES.  HOWEVER,
/	   THE /8 AND /9 SWITCHES ARE NEEDLESSLY REMOVED; AT THE PRESENT TIME THESE
/	   SWITCHES HAVE NO MEANING WITHIN THE "BIN" UTILITY.  [NOTE: REMOVING THE /1
/	   THROUGH /7 SWITCHES IS THE PREFERRED METHOD; SOME PROGRAMS USE WEAKER CODE
/	   THAT MERELY LOCATES THE LOWEST SWITCH IN THE RANGE OF /0 THROUGH /7 SET YET
/	   ALLOWS ANOMALIES.  WHEN THOSE ROUTINES ARE REWRITTEN, THIS CODE WILL BE
/	   MANDATORY TO AVOID ERROR MESSAGES CAUSED BY USERS ATTEMPTING TO USURP THE
/	   LIMITATIONS OF THE "GET" COMMAND.

/	3) NO OTHER OPTIONAL COMMAND SWITCH HAS BEEN CONSIDERED FOR THE PURPOSE OF
/	   BEING FORCED OFF.  IT IS POSSIBLE A CONFLICT COULD DEVELOP THAT WOULD
/	   SUGGEST THIS CODE BE MADE MORE IDIOT-PROOF.  PAPER-TAPE OPTION CHECKING IN
/	   A MORE COMPREHENSIVE MANNER COULD CHANGE THIS.  FOR EXAMPLE, PAPER-TAPE
/	   OPTIONS ARE USELESS ON MACHINES THAT CANNOT HAVE PAPER-TAPE HARDWARE SUCH
/	   AS THE VT-78 AND ALL DECMATES.  HOWEVER, IN THEORY THERE ARE INTERSIL
/	   INTERCEPT I SYSTEMS WITH ASR-33 TELETYPES ATTACHED.

/	4) IT IS CONCEIVABLE THAT PUNCH SUPPORT COULD BE GENERALIZED TO VARIOUS SERIAL
/	   OUTPUT PORTS NORMALLY ASSOCIATED WITH SERIAL PRINTER SUPPORT IN CERTAIN
/	   QUITE NON-STANDARD SITUATIONS.  AN ALTERNATIVE COULD BE TO EXPAND THE
/	   LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY SUPPORT TO INCLUDE A DESIGNATED HIGH-SPEED READER
/	   AND PUNCH.  THIS KIND OF UTILITY IS LIKELY BEST SERVED VIA AN INDEPENDENT
/	   UTILITY MORE LIKE OS/8 PIP WHERE NO IMBEDDED COMPATIBILITY IS IMPLIED OR
/	   NECESSARY.

/	5) AN ISSUE TO CONFIRM: WHEN THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ENABLED WHILE THE
/	   SLURP LOADER IS IN EFFECT, THE /I SWITCH-INITIATED DEVICE HANDLER RELOAD
/	   MUST REAPPLY THE COMPLETE SET OF OVERLAY-SPECIFIC MODIFICATIONS.  TO
/	   IMPLEMENT THIS, "BIN" CODING MUST REALIZE THIS IS NECESSARY AND CREATE AN
/	   INTERFACE BETWEEN THE SLURP LOADER AND THE OVERLAY SUCH THAT THE STARTING
/	   ADDRESS AND FIELD ARE TRANSFERRED INTO A DEDICATED AREA WITHIN THE OVERLAY.
/	   THE PASSED FIELD AND STARTING ADDRESS INFORMATION WILL THUS BE THE ADDRESS
/	   WITHIN THE OVERLAY WHERE THIS DEFERRED ACTION IS HANDLED AFTER THE SYSTEM
/	   DEVICE HANDLER IS RELOADED AND THEN PATCHED BY THE OVERLAY.  PRESUMABLY, IT
/	   IS NOT THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE OVERLAY TO ALSO ENSURE THE PROPER CONTENTS
/	   OF THE SYSTEM LOADER [SINCE THE OVERLAY IS ONLY AN OPTION].

/	NOTE: AT THE ORIGINAL TIME OF THE WRITING OF THIS CODE, THE LOGICAL CONSOLE
/	OVERLAY WAS IN ITS INFANCY.  NONE OF THESE SUPPORT ISSUES WERE ADDRESSED AT
/	THE TIME.  THE REDESIGNED LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY WILL BE AWARE OF THE SHELL
/	OVERLAY WHICH IN TURN ELIMINATES THE CONCEPT OF A RELOADABLE SYSTEM DEVICE
/	HANDLER.  AS SUCH, SUITABLE CODING TECHNIQUES MAY ALLOW THE AREA OTHERWISE
/	RESERVED FOR THE RESIDENT SHELL COMMUNICATIONS AND INFORMATION AREA TO BE USED
/	FOR RESOLVING SUCH ISSUES THAT CANNOT APPLY TO THE SHELL ENVIRONMENT.  AS
/	SUCH, THIS ALLOWS THE USE OF X5400-X5777 FOR THESE NON-SHELL FUNCTIONS.  THE
/	SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER IS NEVER DISPLACED FROM MEMORY WHILE THE SHELL IS IN
/	EFFECT OTHER THAN PERHAPS DURING CERTAIN REBOOT ACTIVITY.
/	THE "BIN" PROGRAM.

/	THE "BIN" UTILITY SUPPORTS PROGRAM CHAINING FROM "PAL" AND "MAP".  IN THEORY,
/	"BIN" CAN CHAIN TO ITSELF.  ALL CHAIN OPERATIONS START AT ONE ADDRESS HIGHER
/	THAN THE NORMAL STARTING ADDRESS.  AS SUCH, A SAFE CONSTANT FOR EXECUTION IS
/	PLACED AT THE NOMINAL ENTRY POINT TO HANDLE EITHER CASE.  IN THIS CASE, THE
/	CONTENTS IS THE POINTER TO A LOW ADDRESS IN MEMORY, WHICH WILL EXECUTE AS A
/	HARMLESS "AND" INSTRUCTION.

/	DEPENDING ON FURTHER OPERATIONS OF "BIN", IT IS FEASIBLE THAT "BIN" CAN
/	MODIFY THIS WORD TO CHANGE THE LOGICAL FLOW OF THE PROGRAM.  HOWEVER, THIS
/	WOULD REQUIRE A ROUTINE LOADED INTO HIGH MEMORY TO DIRECT THE SYSTEM DEVICE
/	HANDLER TO RELOAD THE CORE-IMAGE OF "BIN" FIRST.  FORTUNATELY, THE ENTIRE
/	"BIN" PROGRAM IS SMALL ENOUGH TO ACCOMPLISH THIS. [NOTE: IF "BIN" WAS AS LONG
/	AS 00000-07577 THIS COULD NOT BE ACCOMPLISHED WITHOUT DESTROYING THE PASSED
/	FILE AREA.]

/	THE ONLY EXPECTED FUNCTIONALITY INVOLVING CHAINING IS TO CREATE BINARY OUTPUT
/	FILES FROM BINARY PAPER-TAPE INPUT, THEN IF THE /G SWITCH IS EITHER SET OR
/	IMPLIED, CHAINING BACK TO "BIN" WITH THESE FILES IN THE PASSED FILE AREA AS
/	INPUT FILES FOR LOADING PURPOSES [COMPLETE WITH ALL RELEVANT LOADING OPTIONS
/	AS CAN BE EXPRESSED USING NON-CONFLICTING OPTION SWITCHES].  BY CAREFUL
/	DESIGN, IT IS POSSIBLE TO ACCOMPLISH THIS WITHOUT HAVING TO RELOAD THE PROGRAM
/	IMAGE.  THIS COULD INVOLVE INITIAL PARSING OF CERTAIN PROGRAM OPTIONS IN A
/	DEFERRED MANNER TO BE ACTED UPON WHEN THE INTERNAL SELF-CHAIN OPERATION
/	COMMENCES, ETC.  FAILING THIS, THE "BIN" UTILITY COULD REQUIRE A FULL-FLEDGED
/	RELOAD WITH ALL APPROPRIATE SWITCHES AND FILES PASSED ACCORDINGLY.  THUS, IT
/	IS HIGHLY DESIRABLE TO ATTEMPT TO CREATE THIS DEFERRED OPERATION IF AT ALL
/	POSSIBLE.  HOWEVER, BE ADVISED THAT PROGRAM OPTIONS COULD OVERWHELM THE DESIGN
/	REQUIRING THE DESIGN TO BE RECAST AS ONE THAT SWAPS IN A NEW IMAGE OF THE
/	ENTIRE PROGRAM.

/	"BIN" OPERATION MODES.

/	1) PLACE BIN AND RIM IN MEMORY WITH THE REBOOT CODE AT 07600.  ASSUMING THE
/	   REBOOT CODE IS NOT COMPROMISED, P?S/8 CAN BE RELOADED BY RESTART AT 07600.
/	   THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS ARE AVAILABLE FOR MANUAL OPERATIONS; EITHER CAN BE
/	   STARTED BY THE PROPER USE OF MODIFIER SWITCHES SUCH AS /R TO START IN THE
/	   RIM LOADER STARTING ADDRESS, OR OMIT THE /R SWITCH TO START IN THE BIN
/	   LOADER INTERNAL STARTING ADDRESS [OR 07777, THE OFFICIAL BIN STARTING
/	   ADDRESS].

/	2) CREATE BINARY OUTPUT FILES FROM BINARY PAPER-TAPES.  IN THIS MODE, THE BIN
/	   OR RIM LOADER IS MODIFIED TO PASS ASSEMBLED 12-BIT WORDS MEANT TO BE 
/	   DIRECTLY LOADED INTO MEMORY TO A ROUTINE TO CREATE BINARY OUTPUT FILE
/	   STREAMS PASSED FROM THE COMMAND-LINE PROCESSOR.

/	3) PUNCH BIN OR RIM FORMAT PAPER-TAPES FROM PASSED BINARY INPUT FILES.  A
/	   DESIRABLE FEATURE WOULD BE TO VALIDATE PASSED FILES AS VALID BINARY; ALL
/	   VALID P?S/8 FILES START WITH THE INTERNAL CODING FOR "*200".  AS SUCH, THE
/	   INITIAL CONTROL WORD SHOULD BE MASKED AGAINST 6000 WITH THE RESULT 2000
/	   INDICATING THE FOLLOWING WORD IS AN ORIGIN SETTING; THE NEXT WORD MUST BE
/	   0200.  ERROR MESSAGES CAN BE ISSUED IF INVALID FILES ARE PASSED.  [NOTE:
/	   IT MUST BE CONFIRMED THAT ALL OUTPUT FILES PRODUCED BY THE "PAL" PROGRAM
/	   ACTUALLY CONFORM TO THIS CONVENTION.]

/	4) LOAD PASSED BINARY INPUT FILES SUBJECT TO THE VARIOUS LOADING AND STARTUP
/	   OPTIONS.

/	5) SAME AS 2) ABOVE WITH THE /G SWITCH SET OR IMPLIED.  THE CREATED OUTPUT
/	   FILE LIST IS CONVERTED TO AN INPUT FILE LIST AND PROCEED AS IN 4) ABOVE.

/	6) SAME AS 3) ABOVE WITH THE /F SWITCH SET OR IMPLIED; PROCEED AS IN 4) ABOVE.

/	THE PROGRAM IS ENTERED HERE IF INVOKED AS "BIN".

ZZ2011,	A225				/HERE IN CASE WE'RE CHAINED TO; ALSO POINTER
					/ADDRESS USED ONCE-ONLY BY "START" PROGRAM.
	TAD I	PSCORE/(SCORE)		/GET THE LOGICAL CORE SIZE WORD.
	AND	L70/(70)		/JUST CURRENT LOGICAL SIZE BITS.
	CLL RTR;STL CMA RAR		/INVERT AND FORM - [HOW MANY EXTENDED MEMORY
					/FIELDS TO FILL + 1]
	DCA	FILCNT			/SAVE FOR OPTIONAL EXTENDED MEMORY FILL LATER.
	TAD I	PSLDBLK/[SLDBLK]	/GET BIN PROGRAM'S LOADING BLOCK.
	TAD	ZZ0064
	DCA I	ZZ0152
	TAD I	PSLDBLK/[SLDBLK]	/GET BIN PROGRAM'S LOADING BLOCK AGAIN.
	TAD	ZZ0051
	DCA	ZZ0152


