/	P?S/8 BOOTSTRAP AND SLURP LOADER FOR TC01/TC08 DECTAPE.

/	SLURP LOADER IMBEDDED BOOTSTRAP CONSIDERATIONS.

/	THE FOLLOWING 128-WORD PAGE IS THE COMPLETE DEFINITION OF THE SLURP LOADER FOR
/	THE TC01/TC08 DECTAPE.  THIS INCLUDES THE PASSED INPUT FILE LIST AND ALL
/	PARAMETERS THAT APPLY WHEN THE "BIN" UTILITY LOADS THE CODE INTO 07600-07777
/	FOR THE PURPOSE OF LOADING BINARY FILES.

/	SPECIFIC MEMORY LOCATIONS ARE DESIGNATED AS THE MAXIMUM LENGTH OF A
/	STAND-ALONE BOOTSTRAP FOR THE CORRESPONDING P?S/8 [OR OTHER
/	BOOTSTRAP-COMPATIBLE] OPERATING SYSTEM BASED ON THE SAME HARDWARE.

/	THE CURRENT BOOTSTRAP IS DEFINED AS THE CONTENTS OF 07600-07642 TO BE STARTED
/	AT 07600.  [NOTE: THE ACTUAL CODE NEEDED TO REBOOT THE TC01/TC08 VERSION OF
/	P?S/8 IS SOMEWHAT SHORTER THAN THIS DEFINITION; THE CODE SIZE CAN BE REDUCED
/	FURTHER IF FUTURE DESIGN CHANGES ARE MADE; POTENTIAL ISSUES INCLUDE TRADE-OFFS
/	OF OVERALL SLURP LOADER SIZE VERSUS FUNCTIONALITY.]

/	WHEN THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY LOADS THE PAPER-TAPE BIN AND RIM LOADERS INTO
/	07643-07777, THE SAME BOOTSTRAP CODE WILL BE LOADED INTO 07600-07642; THE
/	THREE COMPONENTS ARE DESIGNED TO COEXIST IN 07600-07777.  [NOTE: SPECIFIC
/	COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS TO "BIN" WILL LOAD AND START THE BIN OR RIM LOADER
/	INSTEAD OF THE SLURP LOADER.]

/	SPECIFIC MEMORY ALLOCATION FOR THE BOOTSTRAP-ONLY PORTION OF THE SLURP LOADER
/	MAY VARY WITH OVERALL RELEASE OF P?S/8.  CONTRADICTORY FACTORS INCLUDE:

/	1) THE LARGEST SIZE CONTIGUOUS CODE REQUIRED TO BOOTSTRAP THE MOST CUMBERSOME
/	   DEVICE.  WHILE THE TC01/TC08 BOOTSTRAP SIZE IS NOT AT ISSUE, THE ANALOGOUS
/	   CODING FOR OTHER DEVICES MAY REQUIRE MORE MEMORY.

/	2) IMPLEMENTATION RESTRICTIONS WITHIN THE P?S/8 VERSION OF THE BIN LOADER ARE
/	   SUBJECT TO CHANGE; CERTAIN CONTEMPLATED MODIFICATIONS COULD LENGTHEN OR
/	   SHORTEN THE PROGRAM DEPENDING ON SPECIFIC GOALS.  THE CURRENT P?S/8
/	   IMPLEMENTATION OF THE BINARY LOADER IS LESS PRONE TO INTERNAL CORRUPTION
/	   PROBLEMS CAUSED BY THREE-CYCLE DATA BREAK DEVICES THAN THE DEC STANDARD
/	   RELEASE [DEC-08-LBAA, 1967].  SHORTENING THE BOOTSTRAP DEFINITION BY ONE
/	   WORD WOULD ELIMINATE THE ONLY KNOWN PROBLEM WHILE MAINTAINING THE CURRENT
/	   FEATURE SET.  [NOTE: FOR MORE INFORMATION, REFER TO DOCUMENTATION OF THE
/	   P?S/8 IMPLEMENTATION OF THE BIN LOADER WITHIN THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY.]

/	LOADING THE BOOTSTRAP CODE MAINTAINS SEEMLESS COMPATIBILITY WITH THE
/	CORRESPONDING P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER WHICH IS DISPLACED.  [NOTE: THE REST
/	OF THE PAGE IS LOADED WITH EITHER THE REST OF THE SLURP LOADER OR THE BIN AND
/	RIM LOADERS DEPENDING ON COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS PASSED TO THE "BIN" UTILITY.]

/	[NOTE: THE TC01/TC08 BOOTSTRAP DESCRIBED HERE IS A STAND-ALONE PROGRAM LOADED
/	ENTIRELY IN FIELD 0.  BY DESIGN, CERTAIN SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLERS REQUIRE
/	EXTENDED MEMORY TO OPERATE.  IN MANY SUCH CASES, MOST OF THE SYSTEM RESTART
/	CODE MAY BE RESIDENT IN EXTENDED MEMORY REQUIRING ONLY A SHORT LINKAGE ROUTINE
/	IN FIELD 0 TO INITIATE THE RESTART.  FUTURE RELEASES OF THE "BIN" UTILITY
/	COULD SUPPORT A UNIVERSAL RESTART CONVENTION FOR ALL SYSTEMS REQUIRING
/	EXTENDED MEMORY; GENERIC INITIALIZATION CODE WOULD BE REQUIRED TO SET THE
/	PROPER MEMORY FIELD INSTRUCTIONS.]
/	BIN AND RIM LOADER FEATURE CONSIDERATIONS.

/	SINCE THE BOOTSTRAP CONSIDERATIONS DISCUSSED ABOVE DEPEND ON FEATURES OF THE
/	STAND-ALONE BIN AND RIM LOADERS, A BRIEF DISCUSSION OF THE ISSUES FOLLOWS:

/	1) DEPENDING ON SPECIFIC COMMAND LINE SWITCHES TO THE "BIN" UTILITY, BINARY
/	   FILES CAN BE LOADED BY THE HARDWARE-DEPENDENT SLURP LOADER OR THE
/	   DEVICE-INDEPENDENT VIRTUAL LOADER.  ALTERNATIVELY, BINARY PAPER-TAPES CAN
/          BE LOADED BY STAND-ALONE VERSIONS OF THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS.

/	2) BOTH PAPER-TAPE LOADERS ARE PRE-CONFIGURED FOR A CHOICE OF EITHER LOW-SPEED
/	   OR HIGH-SPEED READER HARDWARE.  COMPLETE FUNCTIONALITY IS AVAILABLE ON
/	   SYSTEMS LACKING A FRONT PANEL.  [NOTE: THE STAND-ALONE FEATURE OF READER
/	   DEVICE CHOICE WITHIN THE BIN LOADER VIA FRONT PANEL SWITCH[0] HAS BEEN
/	   ELIMINATED; THE "BIN" UTILITY CONFIGURES THE LOADERS DIRECTLY PRIOR TO
/	   FINAL PLACEMENT IN MEMORY DISPLACING THE P?S/8 SYSTEM RESIDENT AREA.]

/	3) P?S/8 ALSO PROVIDES A BOOTSTRAP TO RELOAD THE OPERATING SYSTEM.  WHEN THE
/	   BIN AND RIM LOADERS ARE LOADED OVER THE P?S/8 SYSTEM RESIDENT AREA, THE
/	   APPROPRIATE HARDWARE-DEPENDENT BOOTSTRAP IS LOADED INTO LOCATION 07600 AND
/	   FOLLOWING TO ALLOW P?S/8 TO BE RELOADED BY RESTART AT 07600.  [NOTE: THIS
/	   FUNCTIONALITY DEPENDS ON MAINTAINING BOOTSTRAP CODE INTEGRITY; ROGUE
/	   PROGRAMS COULD CORRUPT THE BOOTSTRAP BY IMPROPERLY LOADING OVER LOCATIONS
/	   07600-07642.]

/	4) WHEN INVOKING ANY BINARY LOADER FROM THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY, THERE IS AN
/	   OPTIONAL FEATURE TO PRELOAD ALL USER MEMORY WITH EITHER 0000 [THE LINC
/	   "HLT" INSTRUCTION] OR 7402 [THE PDP-8 "HLT" INSTRUCTION.].  MAKING USE OF
/	   THIS FEATURE IS STRONGLY RECOMMENDED DURING EARLY PROGRAM DEVELOPMENT.

/	[NOTE: THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY HAS OTHER ADDITIONAL FEATURES BESIDES BINARY
/	LOADING [SUCH AS CONVERTING BINARY FILES TO PAPER-TAPE AND VICE VERSA].  FOR
/	MORE INFORMATION, SEE SEPARATE DOCUMENTATION OF THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY.]

/	SLURP LOADER ERROR CONSIDERATIONS.

/	THE SLURP LOADER USES A SIMPLIFIED DECTAPE SEARCH ROUTINE THAT CANNOT RECOVER
/	FROM DETECTED ERRORS.  SINCE NO BINARY FILE IS EVER LOCATED NEAR AN END ZONE,
/	END ZONE ERRORS SHOULD NOT OCCUR.  ANY OTHER ERRORS SHOULD BE CONSIDERED AS
/	HARDWARE FAILURES THAT MUST BE ADDRESSED WITH SOME FORM OF HARDWARE OR MEDIA
/	MAINTENANCE.  IF THIS IS NOT IMMEDIATELY FEASIBLE, THE /V COMMAND-LINE OPTION
/	SWITCH SHOULD BE USED TO INVOKE THE HARDWARE-INDEPENDENT VIRTUAL LOADER
/	INSTEAD OF THE SLURP LOADER.  ALL DEVICE ERRORS ARE RECOVERABLE WHEN USING THE
/	VIRTUAL LOADER; HOWEVER, THERE ARE MANY TRADE-OFFS.  NOTE: USE OF THE VIRTUAL
/	LOADER IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR PROPER PHYSICAL MAINTENANCE!  OCCURRENCE OF
/	FREQUENT ERRORS IS A SIGN OF A SERIOUS HARDWARE PROBLEM THAT WILL ONLY TEND TO
/	GET WORSE WITH TIME AND USAGE.

/	FUTURE VERSIONS OF THE SLURP LOADER MAY INTERACT WITH THE LOGICAL CONSOLE
/	OVERLAY TO PROVIDE ERROR RECOVERY; THIS WILL DEPEND ON SOME REDESIGN OF BOTH
/	THE "BIN" UTILITY AS WELL AS THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY ITSELF.
	PAGE				/START ON A NEW PAGE.

	SLRPAG=.			/THIS ADDRESS WITHIN THE "BIN" PROGRAM.

	RELOC	SBOOT			/WHERE THIS LOADS.

/	THE SYSTEM RESTARTS HERE [07600].

/	THE DATA FIELD MUST BE 00 AND INTERRUPTS SHOULD BE DISABLED.

/	THE AC AND LINK CONTENTS ARE IGNORED.

/	NOTE: ALL CODE ON THIS PAGE IS SPECIFIC TO THE TCO1/TC08 CONFIGURATION.

SL7770,	SPA SNA SZL CLA/7770		/CLEAR THE AC AND POSSIBLY
					/SKIP; ALSO CONSTANT 7770.

/	THE FOLLOWING INSTRUCTION MIGHT BE SKIPPED OR HARMLESSLY EXECUTED AS "AND 30".

SL30,	30				/CONSTANT 0030.

/	THE AC IS DEFINITELY CLEAR AT THIS POINT.

	DTLB				/ALL DMA TRANSFERS TO FIELD 0.
	TAD	SL600/(600)		/SETUP FOR REWIND ON UNIT 0.
	JMS	SLWAIT			/WAIT FOR REVERSE END ZONE ERROR.
	TAD	SL7577/(SBOOT-1)	/GET PRE-DECREMENTED POINTER TO RELOAD ADDRESS.
	DCA	CA			/STASH IN THE CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER.

/	THE FOLLOWING INSTRUCTION EXECUTES HARMLESSLY AS "AND I SBOOT" [0600].

SL600,	600				/CONSTANT 0600.

/	THE NEXT INSTRUCTION EXECUTES HARMLESSLY AS "AND I 0" [0400]; ADDITIONALLY,
/	IT MUST BE LOCATED AT 7610 TO FORM ANOTHER CONSTANT USED ELSEWHERE.

	IFNZRO	.&177-10	<ERROR	.>

SL400,	400				/CONSTANT 0400.

	TAD	SL220/(0220)		/GET READ FORWARD FUNCTION VALUE.
	JMS	SLWAIT			/GO WAIT THERE FOR DMA OVERLAY TO TAKE CONTROL
					/AWAY FROM US AND GIVE IT TO THE JUST-READ BOOT
/					/BLOCK CONTENTS.
/	TC01/TC08 BOOTSTRAP DESIGN CONSIDERATIONS.

/	WHEN THE BOOTSTRAP CODE IS INITIATED, THE DECTAPE IS REWOUND INTO THE REVERSE
/	END ZONE.  THE BOOTSTRAP THEN INITIATES A FORWARD READ OPERATION; WHEN
/	PERFORMED IN THIS MANNER, BLOCK 0000 WILL BE TRANSFERRED BY DESIGN.

/	DURING THE TAPE BLOCK DMA TRANSFER, THE CONTENTS OF TAPE BLOCK 0000 GRADUALLY
/	REPLACES THE CODE DEFINED HERE; THE ONLY REQUIREMENT IS THE REPLACEMENT WAIT
/	LOOP CODE MUST BE SUFFICIENTLY COMPATIBLE WITH THE BOOTSTRAP-PROVIDED WAIT
/	LOOP TO ALLOW THE DMA TO COMPLETE PROPERLY [SUBJECT TO POSSIBLE DATA TRANSFER
/	LENGTH ALTERATION ONCE THE WORD COUNT AND CURRENT ADDRESS LOCATIONS
/	[07754-07755] ARE OVERLAID BY THE CORRESPONDING DATA ON THE DECTAPE BLOCK].

/	NOTE: CONFORMING WITH THE TC01/TC08 BOOTSTRAP CONVENTION REQUIRES THE LOOP
/	WAITING FOR THE DONE FLAG BE PLACED IN MEMORY LOCATIONS 07616-07617.

/	VERSIONS OF THIS BOOTSTRAP CODE WRITTEN FOR LATER P?S/8 RELEASES MIGHT SUPPORT
/	EXTENDED BOOTSTRAP FUNCTIONALITY AS A SUPERSET OF THE STANDARD TC01/TC08
/	BOOTSTRAP ROUTINE.  THIS ALLOWS BOOTING TO DRIVES OTHER THAN UNIT 0 TO BE USED
/	AS THE SYSTEM DEVICE.

/	EXTENDED UNIT SUPPORT REQUIRES SUPPLYING A UNIT SELECT VALUE IN THE RANGE OF
/	1000 THROUGH 7000; THE TC01/TC08 HARDWARE REQUIRES UNIT INFORMATION PASSED IN
/	AC[0-2] DURING THE "DTLA" OR "DTXA" OPERATION.  THERE MAY BE ADDITIONAL
/	CONSIDERATIONS AFFECTING OVERALL PROGRAM OPERATION AND CODE EFFICIENCY; THIS
/	WILL BE DEALT WITH IN FUTURE RELEASES OF THIS FILE.

/	[NOTE: TRADE-OFFS EXIST WITH REGARD TO DECTAPE STATUS REGISTER "A" ACCESS.
/	THE "DTLA" OPERATION REQUIRES NO PRIOR KNOWLEDGE OF THE STATUS "A" REGISTER.
/	THE "DTXA" OPERATION UPDATES THE EXISTING STATUS REGISTER INFORMATION VIA AN
/	.XOR. TRANSFER BETWEEN THE AC CONTENTS AND THE REGISTER CONTENTS; END-ZONE
/	HANDLING IS GENERALLY EASIER TO IMPLEMENT USING "DTXA"; THE DIRECTION IS
/	MERELY INVERTED USING THE CONSTANT 0400 WHEN THE END ERROR IS DETECTED.]

/	UNLIKE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER EQUIVALENT, THIS ROUTINE IS ONLY USED TO
/	REBOOT P?S/8 [OR ANY OTHER OPERATING SYSTEM COMPATIBLE WITH THIS BOOTSTRAP
/	CONVENTION].  AS SUCH, IT DOES NOT CHECK FOR ERRORS; WHEN USED TO REWIND THE
/	SYSTEM DECTAPE, THE ERROR FLAG RAISED DUE TO CONTROLLER DETECTION OF THE
/	REVERSE END ZONE.  WHEN USED TO READ BLOCK 0000 MOVING FORWARD OUT OF THE
/	REVERSE END ZONE, THE WAIT LOOP WILL BE OVERLAID BY THE CODE CONTAINED ON
/	BLOCK 0000 ACCORDING TO WELL-ESTABLISHED CONVENTIONS.  ALL MEMORY LOCATIONS
/	OTHER THAN THE WAIT LOOP [WHICH MIGHT LEGITIMATELY BE OVERLAID WITH SLIGHTLY
/	DIFFERENT CODE] ARE EXPECTED TO BE COMPLETELY DIFFERENT AS A RESULT OF THE
/	READ OPERATION; ALL SUBSEQUENT ACTIONS ARE DETERMINED BY THE OPERATING SYSTEM
/	BOOT BLOCK CONTENTS [WHICH ARE LIKELY COMPLETELY DIFFERENT FROM THE REST OF
/	THE CODE LOADED HERE TO IMPLEMENT THE SLURP LOADER].
/	THE WAIT ROUTINE AS DEFINED HERE REQUIRES THE NEW CONTENTS OF THE DECTAPE
/	STATUS REGISTER "A" TO BE PASSED IN THE AC BECAUSE THE "DTLA" INSTRUCTION IS
/	USED.  AS SUCH, THERE IS NO DEPENDENCY ON PRIOR STATUS REGISTER CONTENTS.
/	[NOTE: THERE ARE CERTAIN RESTRICTIONS ON CHANGING PARTICULAR STATUS REGISTER
/	BITS; IF CERTAIN COMBINATIONS OF CHANGES ARE DONE IN AN IMPROPER ORDER, THE
/	RESULT COULD BE UNCONTROLLED TAPE MOTION.]

	SLRPBLK=.			/ALSO USED FOR LATEST SLURP BLOCK VALUE STORAGE.

SLWAIT,	.-.				/WAIT ROUTINE.
	DTLA				/LOAD STATUS "A" REGISTER WITH PASSED
					/FUNCTION BITS, CLEAR AC.
	DCA	WC			/CLEAR WORD COUNT REGISTER NOW IN CASE READING.

/	STANDARD TC01/TC08 DECTAPE WAIT LOOP; COMPATIBLE WITH MANY OPERATING SYSTEMS.

	IFNZRO	7616-.	<ERROR .>	/ENSURE COMPATIBILITY WITH THE STANDARD ADDRESS.

SWAITLP,DTSF				/DECTAPE [OR ERROR] FLAG UP?
	JMP	SWAITLP			/FLAG NOT UP YET, KEEP WAITING FOR IT.

/	IF READING, EXECUTION CONTINUES HERE WITH THE NEW CONTENTS OF MEMORY TAKEN
/	FROM BLOCK 0000 OF THE NOW-BOOTED SYSTEM DECTAPE. [NOTE: OFTEN A SUBROUTINE
/	WITH PRELOADED "RETURN" CONTENTS OVERLAYS THIS CODE.  THE P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE
/	HANDLER USES THIS METHOD TO START UP WHEN BOOTSTRAPPED BY THIS CODE OR
/	EQUIVALENT.]

/	THE NEXT INSTRUCTION EXECUTES HARMLESSLY AS "NOP" [7000]; ADDITIONALLY,
/	IT MUST BE LOCATED AT 7620 TO FORM ANOTHER CONSTANT USED ELSEWHERE.

	IFNZRO	.&177-20	<ERROR	.>

SL7000,	7000				/CONSTANT 7000.
	JMP I	SLWAIT			/RETURN TO CALLER [IF NOT OVERLAID].

SL4002,	4002				/CONSTANT 4002.
SL7577,	SBOOT-1				/CONSTANT 7577.

/	NOTE: THE BOOTSTRAP CODE IS COMPLETELY CONTAINED ABOVE WITH THE EXCEPTION OF
/	THE CONSTANT 0220 ["SL220"] DEFINED BELOW.  REWORKING THE CODE CAN SHORTEN THE
/	REQUIREMENT IF NECESSARY; HOWEVER, THERE COULD BE CODE SPACE TRADE-OFFS.

/	THE SLURP LOADER COMES HERE TO STOP THE TAPE AFTER THE LATEST FILE HAS BEEN
/	COMPLETELY LOADED.

SLPSTP,	TAD	SL220/(0220)		/GET READ FUNCTION BITS.
	DTXA				/TURN OFF MOTION BITS [ONLY].

/	THE CODE FALLS THROUGH TO PROCESS THE NEXT FILE [IF ANY].
/	THE SLURP LOADER STARTS HERE AFTER BEING MOVED TO 07600-07777.

SLPSTRT,ISZ	SLFLPTR			/BUMP TO THE NEXT INPUT FILE.
	TAD I	SLFLPTR			/GET LATEST FILE HANDLE [SKIPPED IF AT 7777].
	AND	SL7770/(7770)		/JUST BLOCK BITS.
	SNA				/SKIP IF MORE FILES TO LOAD.
	JMP	SLUSTRT			/ELSE STARTUP THE USER PROGRAM THERE.
	DCA	SLRPBLK			/SAVE FOR SEARCH ROUTINE.
	TAD I	SLFLPTR			/GET LATEST FILE HANDLE AGAIN.
	RTR;RTR				/MOVE UNIT BITS TO AC[0-2].
SL220,	AND	SL7000/(7000)		/ISOLATE UNIT BITS; ALSO CONSTANT 0220.

/	THE ENTIRE STAND-ALONE BOOTSTRAP LOADS ABOVE THIS POINT.  [THE CONSTANT 0220
/	IS USED WITHIN THE BOOTUP CODE.]

	DECTLIM=.			/UPPER LIMIT FOR CURRENT TC01/TC08 BOOTSTRAP.

	TAD	SL210/(210)		/ADD ON FORWARD MOTION AND SEARCH BITS.
	DTLA				/START THE TAPE IN SEARCH MODE, CLEAR AC.

/	SINCE THE AC IS CLEAR, START SEARCHING FORWARD.  IN THE GENERAL CASE THIS
/	WOULD NOT BE RECOMMENDED.  HOWEVER, ALL TFS BINARY FILES [OTHER THAN % AND $]
/	ARE LOCATED FORWARD OF THE CURRENT TAPE POSITION WHERE THE "BIN" UTILITY
/	[WHICH LOADS THIS CODE] IS LOCATED.  LOADING OF ADDITIONAL BINARY FILES COULD
/	CAUSE DOUBLE TAPE TURNAROUNDS FOR EACH FILE DEPENDING ON RELATIVE TAPE
/	POSITION.  THIS CAN BE ELIMINATED BY PLACING UNRELATED FILES BETWEEN FILES
/	TO BE LOADED SEQUENTIALLY; ALL FORWARD SEARCHES WILL THEN ALWAYS LOCATE THE
/	STARTING BLOCK OF EVERY FILE WITHOUT TURNAROUND. [TFS FILES ARE PLACED FURTHER
/	APART THAN THE BLOCK SPACING REQUIRED TO RESTART THE DECTAPE ONCE THE MOTION
/	BIT IS TURNED OFF.] AN EXAMPLE FOLLOWS:

/	.CATALOG:0

/	BFILE1	TEXT07	BFILE2	TEXT08
/	BFILE3	TEXT3A	BFILE4	TEXT3R
/	BFILE5	TXTHLP	BFILE6	MYPROG

/	.BIN BFILE1,BFILE2,BFILE3,BFILE4,BFILE5,BFILE6=200

/	AFTER THE OPERATING SYSTEM LOADS THE "BIN" UTILITY [AND THIS SLURP LOADER
/	CODE], A FORWARD SEARCH WILL FIND "BFILE" WITHOUT TURNING THE TAPE AROUND.
/	SINCE EACH TFS FILE IS 16 BLOCKS LONG, THERE IS A 16 BLOCK SPACING BETWEEN THE
/	BINARY FILES PROVIDED BY THE UNRELATED FILES.  THIS EXCEEDS THE DECTAPE
/	COASTING OFFSET REQUIREMENT WHEN SETTING TAPE MOTION.  NOTE: TAPE MOTION IS
/	CLEARED AFTER EACH FILE IS PROCESSED.  THIS IS NORMAL PRACTICE AS EACH FILE IS
/	AN INDEPENDENT SET OF BLOCKS TO PROCESS; THE NEXT INPUT FILE COULD BE LOCATED
/	ON A DIFFERENT DECTAPE DRIVE UNIT.

/	ADJACENT FILES REQUIRE SUBSEQUENT FILES BE SEARCHED INITIALLY IN REVERSE DUE
/	TO INERTIAL ROLL AFTER THE CONTROLLER CLEARS THE MOTION BIT.  BY UTILIZING
/	FILE INTERLEAVING, THE ENTIRE OPERATION LOADS ALL FILES WITHOUT TAPE
/	TURNAROUND.  [NOTE: THE TAPE SEARCH ROUTINE IS CAPABLE OF REVERSE SEARCH IF
/	NECESSARY; THE SPECIFIC CONSIDERATION DISCUSSED ONLY REFERS TO THE INITIAL
/	SEARCH DIRECTION.]
/	SLURP-SPECIFIC TC01/TC08 DECTAPE BLOCK SEARCH ROUTINE.

/	AT THIS POINT THE TAPE IS MOVING FORWARD IN SEARCH MODE LOOKING FOR THE LATEST
/	DESIRED BLOCK. [NOTE: UNLIKE GENERAL-PURPOSE SEARCH ROUTINES THAT START THE
/	SEARCH BACKWARDS, IT IS KNOWN THAT THE FIRST BLOCK BEING SEARCHED FOR IS THE
/	STARTING BLOCK OF A TFS FILE.  ALL TFS FILES ARE STORED FURTHER DOWN THE TAPE
/	FROM THE "BIN" UTILITY THUS THIS IS THE CORRECT INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION IN
/	THIS PARTICULAR CASE.]

/	THE CAPABILITY OF THIS SEARCH ROUTINE IS FAR LESS THAN THE ONE USED IN THE
/	SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER:

/	1) THERE IS NO CHECK FOR ERRORS SINCE THERE SHOULD NEVER BE AN END ERROR.
/	   [BLOCKS 0002 AND LOWER ARE NOT VALID TAPE BLOCKS FOR TFS BINARY FILES OR
/	   THE "%" AND "$" FILES.]

/	2) DECTAPE BLOCK NUMBERS ONLY USE 11 SIGNIFICANT BITS.  WITHOUT THE NEED TO
/	   PROCESS VERY LOW BLOCK NUMBERS [AND SEARCHING OUT OF THE REVERSE END ZONE]
/	   IT IS ADEQUATE TO SEARCH FOR HIGHER BLOCK NUMBERS USING SIGNED ARITHMETIC.
/	   THE USUAL UNDERSHOOT FACTOR IS USED IN CASE THE DESIRED BLOCK IS LOWER THAN
/	   THE PRESENT DECTAPE POSITION; HOWEVER, THE END ZONE CONDITION NEVER OCCURS
/	   IN ANY VALID SLURP LOADER SEARCH SITUATION.

/	NOTE: ALL ERRORS ARE FATAL.  IF THERE ARE HARDWARE CONSIDERATIONS THAT PREVENT
/	THE USE OF THE SLURP LOADER, THE USER IS DIRECTED TO USE THE VIRTUAL LOADER
/	[ADD THE /V OPTION SWITCH WHEN INVOKING "BIN"] WHICH WILL REQUIRE WRITE ENABLE
/	TO FINISH LOADING [AND TAKE SOMEWHAT MORE TIME TO LOAD THE SAME BINARY FILES];
/	HOWEVER, ALL OPERATIONS LEADING TO ERRORS CAN BE RETRIED.  THIS SHOULD BE
/	CONSIDERED A TEMPORARY MEASURE AS THE OCCURRENCE OF EXCESSIVE ERRORS IS A
/	SIGN OF FAILING HARDWARE [TAPE GUIDES OR DECTAPES] OR LACK OF PROPER
/	MAINTENANCE [SKEW ALIGNMENT ADJUSTMENT OR TAPE AND GUIDE CLEANING].

/	COMES HERE DURING THE SEARCH AFTER FINDING A BLOCK OTHER THAN THE DESIRED ONE.

SLOOP,	SPA CLA				/SKIP IF POSITIVE AC.

/	FOR THE BENEFIT OF THE BIN AND RIM LOADER USAGE, ALL BOOTSTRAP CODE MUST LOAD
/	BEFORE THIS POINT.  [NOTE: EASILY MET IN THE CASE OF TC01/TC08 DECTAPE.]

	BOOTLIM=.			/UPPER LIMIT OF CODE DEFINED IN THE BOOTSTRAP.

	TAD	SL400/(400)		/GET DIRECTION REVERSING BIT
NXTSRCH,DTXA				/POSSIBLY REVERSE DIRECTION BY .XOR.
					/INTO STATUS REGISTER "A"; CLEAR DONE FLAG.
	TAD	SL7750/(7750)		/GET SEARCH BUFFER ADDRESS VALUE.
	DCA	CA			/SETUP CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER FOR SEARCH.
	DTSF!DTRB			/WAIT FOR LATEST BLOCK; ALSO CHECK FOR ERRORS.
	JMP	.-1			/WAIT UNTIL THE DONE [OR ERROR] FLAG RAISES.
 	SPA				/SKIP IF NO ERRORS.
	HLT				/HALT IF A TAPE ERROR [NOT RECOVERABLE].

/	AT THIS POINT THE LATEST TAPE BLOCK HAS BEEN FOUND WITHOUT ERRORS.  NOTE:
/	AC[3] IS CLEAR BECAUSE A SELECT ERROR DID NOT OCCUR.
	DTRA				/GET STATUS REGISTER "A".
SL210,	AND	SL400/(400)		/JUST CURRENT DIRECTION BIT.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF GOING FORWARDS.
	TAD	SL4002/(4002)		/ADD ON UNDERSHOOT FACTOR IF GOING IN REVERSE.
	TAD	SRCHBLK			/GET LATEST BLOCK FOUND.
	CIA				/INVERT AND
	TAD	SLRPBLK			/COMPARE TO DESIRED BLOCK.
	SZA				/SKIP IF AT THE DESIRED BLOCK.
	JMP	SLOOP			/SIGN BIT WILL DETERMINE TAPE DIRECTION THERE.

/	THE DESIRED BLOCK HAS BEEN FOUND WHILE MOVING FORWARD; SWITCH TO READ MODE.

	TAD	SL30/(30)		/GET NEW FUNCTION BITS.
	DTXA				/.XOR. INTO THE FUNCTION REGISTER TO START READ.

/	EACH DATA WORD TRANSFER WILL BE MONITORED INDIVIDUALLY.  SLURP FILE
/	PARTICULARS WILL BE DEALT WITH IN REAL-TIME.

/	SLURP FORMAT DETAILS.

/	EVERY BLOCK OF A SLURP FILE IS INDEPENDENT OF ALL OTHER BLOCKS OTHER THAN ANY
/	CONSIDERATION OF CURRENT LOADING ORIGIN AND CURRENT LOADING FIELD.

/	THERE ARE 18 GROUPS OF SEVEN WORDS.  EACH GROUP CONSISTS OF A CONTROL WORD
/	THAT DETERMINES THE DISPOSITION OF THE SIX WORDS THAT FOLLOW.  ANY ADDITIONAL
/	WORDS WIHIN THE BLOCK ARE IGNORED.

/	EACH CONTROL WORD CONTAINS SIX PAIRS OF CONTROL BITS, EACH FOR THE
/	CORRESPONDING DATA WORD.  [BIT PAIRS ARE RECKONED LEFT TO RIGHT.]

/	WITHIN EACH PAIR OF BITS, THE FOLLOWING DEFINITIONS APPLY:

/	00 - THIS WORD IS DATA TO BE LOADED INTO THE LOCATION POINTED TO BY THE
/	     LOADING ORIGIN; THE LOADING ORIGIN WILL BE INCREMENTED AFTERWARDS.

/	10 - THIS WORD IS AN ORIGIN SETTING; LOAD THE VALUE INTO THE LOADING ORIGIN.

/	11 - THIS WORD IS A FIELD SETTING EXPRESSED AS A "CDF" INSTRUCTION TO THE NEW
/	     LOADING FIELD; THE VALUE WILL BE STORED IN-LINE WITHIN THE SLURP LOADER;
/	     NEW DATA [IF ANY] WILL BE LOADED INTO THIS FIELD.

/	01 - END OF FILE HAS BEEN DETECTED; IGNORE ALL ADDITIONAL DATA WORDS IN THIS
/	     DATA BLOCK AND ANY ADDITIONAL BLOCKS IN THE FILE.
/	PROCESS THE LATEST BINARY BLOCK IN SLURP FORMAT.

	TAD	SL7756/(-22)		/SETUP THE
	DCA	GRPCTR			/GROUP COUNTER.
NXTGRP,	TAD	SL7772/(-6)		/SETUP THE LATEST
	DCA	GWRDCTR			/GROUP WORD COUNTER.
	JMS	GETWRD			/GET LATEST GROUP CONTROL WORD.
	CLL RAR				/MOVE OVER INITIALLY.
	SKP				/DON'T USE PREVIOUS GROUP CONTROL WORD.
NXTWRD,	TAD	SLPTEMP			/GET LATEST CONTROL WORD.
	RTL				/MOVE OVER TO PROCESS LAST DATA WORD.
	DCA	SLPTEMP			/STORE BACK FOR NEXT TIME.
	TAD	SLPTEMP			/GET THE UPDATED GROUP CONTROL WORD.
	SPA CLA				/SKIP IF DATA OR ORIGIN SETTING.
	JMP	FLDCHK			/JUMP IF FIELD SETTING OR END-OF-FILE.
	JMS	GETWRD			/GET A FILE WORD
SLPFLD,	CDF	00+.-.			/WILL BE "CDF" TO THE LOADING FIELD.
	SNL				/SKIP IF AN ORIGIN SETTING
	DCA I	SLRPORG			/STORE DATA WORD.
	CDF	00			/BACK TO FIELD 0.
	ISZ	SLRPORG			/BUMP TO NEXT LOADING LOCATION.
	SZL				/SKIP IF DATA WORD
	DCA	SLRPORG			/STORE NEW LOADING ORIGIN.
SLPNEXT,ISZ	GWRDCTR			/FINISHED THIS GROUP?
	JMP	NXTWRD			/NO, GO PROCESS NEXT WORD.
	ISZ	GRPCTR			/YES, FINISHED ALL GROUPS IN THIS BLOCK?
	JMP	NXTGRP			/NO, GO BACK AND DO ANOTHER ONE.

/	ALL RELEVANT DATA WORDS ON THIS BLOCK HAVE BEEN PROCESSED; THE REST OF THE
/	BLOCK WILL BE IGNORED; NOW PROCESS THE NEXT BLOCK IN THE CURRENT FILE.

	ISZ	SLRPBLK			/BUMP TO NEXT BLOCK.
	TAD	SL30/(30)		/GET FUNCTION BITS TO CHANGE MODE TO SEARCH.
	JMP	NXTSRCH			/SEARCH FOR THE NEXT FILE BLOCK.

/	COMES HERE TO CHECK FOR FIELD SETTING OR END-OF-FILE.

FLDCHK,	SNL CLA				/SKIP IF FIELD SETTING.
	JMP	SLPSTP			/JUMP IF END-OF-FILE.
	JMS	GETWRD			/GET THE "CDF" NEW FIELD INSTRUCTION.
	DCA	SLPFLD			/STORE IN-LINE
	JMP	SLPNEXT			/GO PROCESS THE NEXT WORD.
/	THIS IS THE HEART OF THE SLURP LOADER.  3-CYCLE DATA BREAKS ARE IN PROGRESS.
/	A 12-BIT DATA WORD IS TRANSFERRED EVERY 133 MICROSECONDS. EACH TRANSFER BUMPS
/	UP THE WORD COUNT.  HOWEVER, WE ZERO THE WORD COUNT ON EACH WORD TRANSFER,
/	THEN WAIT FOR THE WORD COUNT TO CHANGE FROM 0000 -> 0001.  THE CURRENT ADDRESS
/	REGISTER IS RESET TO ALWAYS POINT TO THE SAME MEMORY LOCATION, AVOIDING THE
/	NEED FOR A PAGE-LONG BUFFER AND ALLOWING ALL USER SPACE TO BE LOADED WITHOUT
/	ANY RESTRICTIONS.  NOTE: THIS ROUTINE MUST BE CALLED WITH THE AC CLEAR.

GETWRD,	.-.				/GET A WORD ROUTINE.
	DCA	WC			/CLEAR WORD COUNT REGISTER.
	TAD	SL7750/(ONEWORD-1)	/GET POINTER TO ONE-WORD BUFFER.
	DCA	CA			/STASH IN CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER.
WATLUP,	TAD	WC			/GET CURRENT WORD COUNT REGISTER VALUE.
SL7750,	SPA SNA CLA			/SKIP IF IT CHANGED; ALSO CONSTANT 7750.
	JMP	WATLUP			/JUMP BACK IF IT HASN'T CHANGED YET.
	TAD	ONEWORD			/GET THE LATEST DATA WORD.
	JMP I	GETWRD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

SL7756,	7756				/CONSTANT 7756.
SLRPORG,.-.				/SLURP LOADER LOADING ORIGIN.
SLPTEMP,.-.				/SLURP GROUP CONTROL WORD TEMPORARY.

	ZBLOCK	2			/EMPTY SPACE!

/	INVOKING THE SLURP LOADER FROM THE P?S/8 "BIN" UTILITY DOES NOT DEMAND AN
/	EXPLICIT PROGRAM STARTING ADDRESS.  IF GIVEN BY THE USER, "STFLD" AND
/	"SEQUALS" WILL BE SET TO THE STARTING FIELD AS A "CIF CDF" INSTRUCTION AND THE
/	12-BIT STARTING ADDRESS RESPECTIVELY.  THE DEFAULT VALUES ARE "CIF CDF 00" AND
/	"DEFSTRT".  THIS IS THE ADDRESS OF A SAFE HALTING INSTRUCTION.  PRESSING
/	"CONTINUE" WILL ALWAYS LOOP BACK TO THE SAME ADDRESS AS A SAFETY FEATURE.
/	THIS IS IMPLEMENTED BY EITHER A "JMP" INSTRUCTION BACK TO "STFLD" OR PLACING
/	"DEFSTRT" IN THE PREVIOUS MEMORY LOCATION; PRESSING "CONTINUE" WILL CAUSE THE
/	CODE TO FALL THROUGH THUS REPEATING THE DEFAULT STARTING ACTION.

	DEFSTRT=.			/DEFAULT STARTING ADDRESS IF NONE GIVEN.

SL7772,	SPA SNA SZL CLA HLT		/HALTS HERE BY DEFAULT; ALSO CONSTANT 7772.
					/NOTE: THE AC IS ZERO; THIS WILL NOT SKIP.

/	ENSURE THE DEFAULT START IS HERE.

	IFNZRO	SL7772-DEFSTRT	<ERROR	.>

/	THE USER PROGRAM IS STARTED UP HERE AFTER ALL SLURP LOADING IS CONCLUDED.

SLUSTRT,CIF CDF	00+.-.			/WILL BE "CIF CDF" TO STARTING FIELD.
	JMP I	SEQUALS			/GO START IT UP THROUGH THERE.

/	ENSURE THE USER STARTUP IS JUST PAST THE DEFAULT START; PRESSING "CONTINUE"
/	WILL JUST LOOP BACK HARMLESSLY.

	IFNZRO	DEFSTRT-SLUSTRT+1	<ERROR	.>
/	THE POINTER TO THE SEARCH BUFFER [7750] IS ALSO AN "SPA SNA CLA" INSTRUCTION.

	IFNZRO	7750-.	<ERROR	.>

	GWRDCTR=.			/ALSO USED AS GROUP WORD COUNTER IN DATA MODE.

SRCHBLK,.-.				/BLOCK MARKS TRANSFER HERE IN SEARCH MODE.

/	THE SLURP LOADER CONSTANTLY RESETS THE CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER TO FORCE ALL
/	DATA TRANSFERS INTO THE SAME ONE-WORD BUFFER.

	IFNZRO	7751-.	<ERROR	.>	/DATA BREAK WORDS TRANSFER HERE IN READ MODE.

ONEWORD,.-.				/ONE WORD DATA BUFFER.

/	BY PLACING THE SEARCH MODE BLOCK MARK BUFFER ONE BEFORE THE CONTINUOUSLY RESET
/	DATA BREAK BUFFER, THE SAME ADDRESS VALUE CAN BE USED TO SETUP THE CURRENT
/	ADDRESS REGISTER WITHIN THE RESPECTIVE ROUTINES. [NOTE: IN SEARCH MODE THE
/	CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER DOES NOT INCREMENT WHILE IN READ MODE THE CURRENT
/	ADDRESS REGISTER INCREMENTS FOR EACH DATA WORD TRANSFERRED.]

	IFNZRO	SRCHBLK-ONEWORD+1	<ERROR	.>

GRPCTR,	.-.				/SLURP BLOCK GROUP COUNTER.
SLFLPTR,SFILES-1			/INPUT FILE LIST POINTER; WILL BE
					/PRE-INCREMENTED BEFORE USE.  THE VALUE
					/WILL BE ADJUSTED FOR PASSED OUTPUT FILES.

/	TC01/TC08 DECTAPE 3-CYCLE DATA BREAK ADDRESSES.

WC,	.-.				/WORD COUNT REGISTER.
CA,	.-.				/CURRENT ADDRESS REGISTER.

SEQUALS,DEFSTRT				/WILL BE 12-BIT STARTING ADDRESS; DEFAULT VALUE
					/IS THE ADDRESS OF THE SAFE HALTING INSTRUCTION.

SFILES,	ZBLOCK	-.			/EMPTY SPACE TO FLESH OUT THE TAPE BLOCK IMAGE.

	IFNZRO	.	<ERROR	.>	/SHOULD NOW BE JUST PAST THE END OF THE PAGE.

	RELOC				/TURN OFF RELOCATION.

	PRGEND=	.			/LOADING ADDRESS UPPER LIMIT FOR "BIN".
/	AS A RELATIVE OFFSET, THIS IS THE LOWEST BLOCK AVAILABLE FOR THE VIRTUAL
/	LOADER'S BUFFER.  THE ENTIRE PROGRAM INCLUDES THE VIRTUAL BUFFER.  THE NEXT
/	PROGRAM IN THE SYSTEM PROGRAM DIRECTORY MUST ACCOUNT FOR THE VIRTUAL BUFFER
/	SINCE IT MUST BE PROTECTED [IT WILL BE WRITTEN ON IF THE VIRTUAL LOADER IS
/	USED].

/	SYSTEM DIRECTORY MAINTENANCE FOR SYSTEM PROGRAMS THAT INCLUDE OVERLAYS OR
/	RESERVED BLOCKS.

/	ORDINARILY THE ENTRY IN THE SYSTEM PROGRAM DIRECTORY IS THE ENTIRE PROGRAM AS
/	USUALLY DEFINED; MOST PROGRAMS LOAD WITH A SINGLE LOADING SEGMENT.  FOR
/	PROGRAMS SUCH AS THIS "BIN" UTILITY, ADDITIONAL BLOCKS MUST BE RESERVED BEYOND
/	THOSE INVOLVED IN THE DIRECTORY ENTRY ITSELF.  KNOWLEDGEABLE USERS CAN
/	MAINTAIN THIS AREA ONLY IF THE IMPLICIT AGGREGATE OFFSET IS KNOWN.  THIS CAN
/	BE ESPECIALLY TROUBLESOME FOR SENTINEL ENTRIES SINCE THERE IS NO WAY TO
/	OBSERVE THE OFFSET DIRECTLY.

/	TO REMEDY THIS, AN INDEPENDENT UTILITY MUST BE CREATED WITH REGISTERED ENTRIES
/	FOR ALL KNOWN SYSTEM PROGRAMS THAT UTILIZE OVERLAY STRUCTURES OR RESERVED
/	BUFFERS.  THIS WILL ALLOW THE PROGRAM THE ABILITY TO DEFINE THE FIRST FREE
/	BLOCK PAST ANY SUCH PROGRAM THAT WOULD NOT BE RESERVED AS A PORTION OF THE
/	PROGRAM; IF THE VERY LAST PROGRAM IN THE DIRECTORY THIS WOULD DEFINE THE FIRST
/	BLOCK FREE IN THE SYSTEM PROGRAM AREA, ETC.  ONLY THE MOST EXPERT USERS SHOULD
/	ATTEMPT TO DEFINE ADDITIONAL SYSTEM PROGRAMS, ESPECIALLY THOSE WHICH ALSO USE
/	OVERLAYS OR RESERVED AREAS AS THIS WOULD REQUIRE AN UPDATED RELEASE OF SUCH A
/	UTILITY, EVEN IF IT ONLY APPLIED TO A SINGLE P?S/8 SYSTEM.  AS LONG AS THERE
/	ARE NO NAME CONFLICTS, THE UTILITY CAN SERVE ALL CASES OTHER THAN THE PERVERSE
/	CASE OF AN UNREGISTERED PROGRAM BEING ADDED AT THE END OF THE DIRECTORY.  ALL
/	EXISTENT PROGRAMS CAN BE CHECKED AGAINST THEIR KNOWN COMPLETE LENGTHS TO
/	DETERMINE IF ANY ENTRIES SEEM TO BE IN CONFLICT.  IF THERE IS SUFFICENT
/	INTEREST, THE MANAGEMENT PROGRAM ITSELF COULD BE DEFINED AS A SYSTEM PROGRAM
/	TO LEND STABILITY TO THE PROCESS.  FOR THE PRESENT, ONLY EXPERTS SHOULD MODIFY
/	THE SYSTEM DIRECTORY AND THE STARTING BLOCK OF ANY FILE DIRECTORY STRUCTURES
/	THAT FOLLOW IT TO PREVENT POTENTIAL PROBLEMS, ETC.

/no!  tHE DIRECTORY HAS A SENTINEL FREE SPACE ENTRY.  bUT STILL HAVE TO WARN ABOUT
/ACTUAL LENGTH OF ANY ENTRY, BUT THAT'S A SMALLER PROBLEM.



/	UTILITY PROGRAMS TO CREATE SYSTEM PROGRAM ENTRIES WILL REQUIRE THIS OFFSET
/	TO PROPERLY MAINTAIN THE SYSTEM DIRECTORY, ESPECIALLY WERE BIN TO BECOME THE
/	LAST PROGRAM ENTR.

	PRGLEN=	PRGEND%200		/LENGTH OF LOADED PROGRAM IN BLOCKS.

/	A PAGE ZERO LOCATION MAY BE IN USE AS THE CONSTANT 0012 IN ABSOLUTE TERMS.  IT
/	IS BEING USED AS THE LENGTH OFFSET TO LOCATE THE VIRTUAL BUFFER AREA WHERE
/	NEEDED.  SHOULD THE PROGRAM BE MODIFIED, THIS WILL CAUSE A LOGIC CONFLICT THAT
/	MAY BE REMEDIED BY SEPARATING THE USAGE TO ALLOW INDEPENDENT USAGE.

/	ENSURE THIS DEPENDENCY IS MAINTAINED.

	IFNZRO	PRGLEN-12	<ERROR.>

